{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil","id":33221,"title":"Is the Syndicate evil?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-19T08:33:24-08:00","id":33221,"title":"Is the Syndicate evil?","content":"I'm finally reading the last of the CB's - Syndicate. And I can't tell if they're evil relatively speaking because IRL I'm pretty much everything they're against, or whether they're objectively bad. I know that while it was hard for me to play 'em back in the day, after reading this new CB it's gonna be all but impossible unless I wanna play someone I see as just downright evil. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T08:49:51-08:00","id":33234,"title":"","content":"With the exception of the Nephandi, no faction is objectively evil. Are there evil people who are members of the Syndicate. Yup. But there are evil members of the Cult of Ecstacy, Dreamspeakers and Verbena too. The Syndicate's goals are to elevate all of humanity using economic opportunities to improve the human condition.<br /> <br /> For all the blame lumped on the United States for its greed and wealth, it also donates more to help others (both individually and as a whole) than every other nation on Earth (one prominent example that came up recently for me was that even though Americans only account for 10% of the total population of Catholics in the world, America is the source for over 60% of the donations to world-wide Catholic charities). Wealth creates opportunities to help others that just wouldn't be possible if someone was struggling to simply get by paycheck to paycheck.<br /> <br /> Money in and of itself is not evil, it's what you DO with that money that matters. Might I suggest a Syndicate member who puts their talents to work fund-raising for cancer research or an Enforcer going after third-world bureaucrats diverting foreign aid funds meant to feed the hungry into their own pockets. There's lots of ways to portray sympathetic Syndicate people, just remember that money is only the TOOL they use to achieve good ends, not the end in and of itself, and it shouldn't be too hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","user":"Chris24601","date":". 12-19-2013, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T09:19:37-08:00","id":33261,"title":"","content":"They're not evil, they're just misguided.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T10:03:12-08:00","id":33279,"title":"","content":"One of my buddies pointed this out to me one day and I realized how much it changed my perspective on The Syndicate. &quot;Uncle&quot; Scrooge McDuck would be a member of The Syndicate. After watching <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0092345/\" target=\"_blank\">DuckTales</a> as a kid, kinda hard to see him as &quot;evil&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T10:05:07-08:00","id":33280,"title":"","content":"The Syndicate is selfish, smug, and deluded as to the value of money and finance. This causes them to do evil. Highly virtueous and noble people with great power can do great harm if they ignore the rights of others and forget to respect others. The Syndicate has vast power, little virtue, and less nobility, and they assume the worst about most of humanity. So they can't correct their errors very well. Then we need to remember the wise words of Doctor Who (an Etherite if their ever was one) &quot;The very powerful and the very stupid have one thing in common. They don't change their opinions to fit the facts, they change the facts to fit their opinions. Which can be inconvient if you're one of the facts that need changing.&quot;<br /> <br /> Most of the Syndicate's worst crimes are attempts to change the facts to fit their opinions. but this is true of most Mages other than Nephandi.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T10:40:31-08:00","id":33296,"title":"","content":"i don't think the Syndicate is innately corrupt and evil, its just that they are in a position of great temptation, and as such have a high potential to be corrupted and become evil. power does that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>there are no bad ideas, just ideas that have not been refined enough","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1608-iamthesweeper","name":"IAmTheSweeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T12:36:19-08:00","id":33344,"title":"","content":"What\u2019s wrong with the Syndicate is the same thing that is wrong with most of the Technocratic Union in general, namely that it is generally set up as a top-down elitist structure and the ones that make it to the top of that structure tend to be the most driven OCD control freaks in the organization. On top of that, each level they are pressured not to fraternize with those in lower positions for operational security and to avoid influence trickling up the structure from \u201cless informed\u201d levels but it has the side effect of isolating the tiers with each level being \u201cus\u201d to those on it and everyone of lower rank being marginalized and lumped into successively lower levels of \u201cthem\u201d who have less access to information and are theoretically are less competent than those above. Eventually they are reduced to nothing but statistics in the eyes of the higher-ups and no one really cares about the details of numbers, just the bottom line.<br /> <br /> They believe in survival of the fittest, that you have to separate the wheat from the chaff, and all those other cutthroat business adages and to advance in the organization one must be ruthless, efficient, and to put it bluntly cheat and not get caught at it. Some call it unpleasant but necessary expediency for the greater good; others call it criminal disregard for the rules and the rights of others. Personally I see it as more the latter which is why I prefer the Traditions even though they are not without their own glaring flaws.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T13:27:40-08:00","id":33368,"title":"","content":"The Syndicate isn't any more evil than all the other Convention. Like with the NWO and the idea of them as jack-booted thought police, the negative aspects of the Syndicate tend to dominant their image but that's but one part of them. One of the best examples of the Syndicate doing something in positive is in the opening and closing fiction of the CB. Yes the Syndicate agent closes down a Prog op to introduce a cure for cancer to the Masses but not because it's a money sink or it's going to cost the Syndicate, she's closing it because the way they're doing it is too dangerous and is a Paradox disaster waiting to happen*. She knows that while the Masses dream of a world without cancer but deep down they know it isn't possible, yet. Hence why what those Progenitors were doing was dangerous, rather than working to inspire Sleeper scientists to fnd the cure through normal science and technology they were helping them with Enlightened Science, cheating the process of getting it accepted by the Masses.<br /> <br /> *Ironically enough that's the same as the Faith Healing and other mystic healing practices that the Traditions have tried giving to the Sleepers, something the Prog hate.<br /> <br /> Before reading the new Syndicate CB I didn't like them, they were easily my least favorite of the Conventions. In earlier works I found them coming off as a group of money-grubbing crooks and accountants. But then I read the book and I realized there's a lot more to them than money. In fact despite what people think, money is just a tool for them. It's easy to miss how they can inspire the Masses, especially compared to the other Conventions, and to think of them at best as pragmatic and down to Earth or at worst... well a purely antagonist force with no redeemable qualities. But you can find the good and inspirational in them if you look close enough at them, just as with any other Convention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T13:31:51-08:00","id":33370,"title":"","content":"I don't think it matters. The Syndicate leaders don't care about your opinions on the matter, and they're the ones who run the world not you. So your options are: compromise and achieve as much 'good' as you feel you can in your own limited way, or your boss can have you send for retraining. Or you could be quiet and work to overthrow the system from the inside, while trying not to be co-opted into that system.<br /> <br /> That said, is it really that hard to play a character with a terrible ideology? I've done it quite a few times, can be quite fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T15:54:01-08:00","id":33475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BC001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=33344#post33344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What\u2019s wrong with the Syndicate is the same thing that is wrong with most of the Technocratic Union in general,...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a problem, though - I can see most of the other Conventions as &quot;good guys.&quot; That's what the whole CB thing is supposed to be about - portraying them as good guys even though they've traditionally been portrayed as bad guys. But the CB:Syndicate... I just can't get my head around them as &quot;good guys.&quot; They still strike me as bad guys even with the obvious attempts to make them good.<br /> <br /> However, judging by the responses above, I guess that might be largely due to my RL politics as opposed to IC stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T16:35:53-08:00","id":33528,"title":"","content":"Correct me if I'm wrong here, but isn't the Syndicate the only Convention of the entire Technocracy that flat doesn't really believe that Ascension is possible. I think that's even mentioned in the Revised Syndicate book that they would much prefer that things stay at the current status quo, which is an elitist plutocracy where they are at the top of things. The rest of Technocracy may have their negative aspects but at least they want to improve humanity as a whole. Yeah, their idea of improvement is similar to the Borg Collective, but at least there everyone is equal and not being treated as wage-slaves.<br /> <br /> But when it comes to the notion of whether the Syndicate is evil I'd have to say not really, relativity speaking anyways. This is World of Darkness were talking about and with guys like the Nephandi, Black Spiral Dancers and Sabbat running around, the Syndicate just looks cute in comparison. Just think about it, which is worse the jackass that pays you minimum wage and uses morally dubious business practices, or the people who worship Cthulhu-Satan, eat babies and masturbate to the idea of murdering the entirety of the human race.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T17:30:49-08:00","id":33562,"title":"","content":"Big Brother: Yeah that's the thing. The Syndicate and the NWO represent Big Business and Big Government both of which in this day and age aren't thought of by most in a positive light while the VE represent exploration, Prog medical science, It-X robotics and general technology, things that are more easier for people understand as good. But just as there is darkness in the latter three* there is light in the former. You just have to look for it. With the NWO it's a little easier to see the good, they're the guys on the Front Lines protecting the Masses from monsters. Yeah the VE protects Earth from alien threats but the NWO is fighting the stuff already here.<br /> <br /> *For instance while the Prog CB is all about healing the Union and the world there is this undercurrent to the book, hinting that if a Convention is going to push for restarting the Pogrom it's them.<br /> <br /> For the Syndicate it's a little trickier. To really get a grasp on their positive side you really have to understand some of core aspects of their Paradigm and Primal Utility. Despite what some say they don't really believe in a Darwinist, survival of the fittest system, they simply believe that while everyone should be given an equal chance to succeed by their own merits not everyone can. After all not everyone can be management, nor should they. And yes, that means that not everyone can Awaken/achieve Enlightenment but that doesn't mean they don't believe people shouldn't try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T22:21:46-08:00","id":33705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Big Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=33475#post33475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a problem, though - I can see most of the other Conventions as &quot;good guys.&quot; That's what the whole CB thing is supposed to be about - portraying them as good guys even though they've traditionally been portrayed as bad guys. But the CB:Syndicate... I just can't get my head around them as &quot;good guys.&quot; They still strike me as bad guys even with the obvious attempts to make them good.<br /> <br /> However, judging by the responses above, I guess that might be largely due to my RL politics as opposed to IC stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to say, I came away from CB: Syndicate the same way: it really didn't change my whole conception of the Convention the way the others did. I thought the Syndicate were money-grubbing assholes going in, and that's pretty much what I thought going out. As propaganda (and the CBs are that, in-character) it was pretty worthless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/740-anaximander","name":"Anaximander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar740_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T07:53:12-08:00","id":33867,"title":"","content":"I think that this <i>is</i> a case of IRL politics getting in the way. I have no problem seeing the \u201clight side\u201d of the Syndicate; though I suspect that by the standards of your IRL politics, <i>my</i> IRL politics would probably qualify as \u201cevil\u201d; so I doubt that my perspective on the matter is going to help you much.<br /> <br /> AkatsukiLeader13 encapsulates some of the more critical points in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=33562#post33562\">his post</a>, though I\u2019d add to that the notion that to the Syndicate\u2019s way of thinking, a healthy economy benefits everyone: so even if you <i>don\u2019t</i> get to be management, that doesn\u2019t mean that the Syndicate doesn\u2019t care what happens to you or wants to turn you into a wage slave. It\u2019s not stated in the Revised CB as clearly as in the original one (because the Revised CB is less about grand visions than the original CB was), but the Syndicate\u2019s vision of \u201cglobal Ascension\u201d is a post-scarcity economy, where it doesn\u2019t <i>matter</i> if there\u2019s inequality, because even the poorest man wants for nothing.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I have more trouble picturing the NWO as benevolent figures. I <i>can</i> do it, by focusing on the \u201cespionage agents\u201d side of their operations and downplaying the \u201cBig Brother\u201d aspect of thought police backing a totalitarian world government; but in general, I\u2019m like the Void Engineers in this regard: if the looming civil war between the NWO and the Syndicate were to actually happen, I\u2019d be more inclined to side with the Syndicate than the NWO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T10:53:11-08:00","id":33962,"title":"","content":"Or to put it more simply, you'd rather have the Blade Runner future (Syndicate) than the 1984 future (NWO)... Meanwhile thr Trekkies (Void Engineers) get completely ignored as head-in-the-clouds idealists by the others... Even though RL NASA scientists think they've now figured out how to make a practical warp drive (it only needs about 700 kg of exotic matter instead of the weight of Jupiter) that could reach Alpha Centauri in about two weeks. The biggest surprise to the NWO and the Syndicate is going to be when the VE's turn both of them into obsolete has beens... The meek will inherit the Earth. The bold will inherit the stars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T17:18:34-08:00","id":34184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=33962#post33962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or to put it more simply, you'd rather have the Blade Runner future (Syndicate) than the 1984 future (NWO)...</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s not putting it more simply; it\u2019s putting it more simplistically. In particular, the Blade Runner future isn\u2019t a post-scarcity economy, and is in fact more of an Iteration X future than a Syndicate one: the primary questions tackled have less to do with economics than with the Man/Machine question. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=33962#post33962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile thr Trekkies (Void Engineers) get completely ignored as head-in-the-clouds idealists by the others... Even though RL NASA scientists think they've now figured out how to make a practical warp drive (it only needs about 700 kg of exotic matter instead of the weight of Jupiter) that could reach Alpha Centauri in about two weeks. The biggest surprise to the NWO and the Syndicate is going to be when the VE's turn both of them into obsolete has beens... The meek will inherit the Earth. The bold will inherit the stars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly agree that a practical FTL Drive would be a game-changer; though I have two caveats: it wouldn\u2019t render the other Conventions obsolete (the NWO and Syndicate would go with humanity to the stars), and what NASA has uncovered isn\u2019t so much a practical warp drive as a theoretical warp drive that isn\u2019t ludicrously impractical on its face: 700 kg of exotic matter is still a problem when you consider that exotic matter is itself entirely theoretical, and that no practical scheme exists for coming up with even 1 kg of it. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T18:35:32-08:00","id":34216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=33867#post33867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AkatsukiLeader13 encapsulates some of the more critical points in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=33562#post33562\">his post</a>, though I\u2019d add to that the notion that to the Syndicate\u2019s way of thinking, a healthy economy benefits everyone: so even if you <i>don\u2019t</i> get to be management, that doesn\u2019t mean that the Syndicate doesn\u2019t care what happens to you or wants to turn you into a wage slave. It\u2019s not stated in the Revised CB as clearly as in the original one (because the Revised CB is less about grand visions than the original CB was), but the Syndicate\u2019s vision of \u201cglobal Ascension\u201d is a post-scarcity economy, where it doesn\u2019t <i>matter</i> if there\u2019s inequality, because even the poorest man wants for nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, the original CB quotes Gordon Gekko from <i>Wall Street</i>--a believer in the zero sum game if there ever was one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T20:42:22-08:00","id":34276,"title":"","content":"Oh, certainly; I\u2019m not denying that the Syndicate has a dark side. But the question posed wasn\u2019t about how evil the Syndicate can get; it was about what redeeming qualities it has. And you don\u2019t look to the Syndicate\u2019s Gordon Gekkos to find its redeeming qualities any more than you\u2019d look to the original Terminator to find Iteration X\u2019s redeeming qualities.<br /> <br /> You want to play the Syndicate as villains? Play them with a zero-sum mentality where everyone they help is offset by someone who is hurt, and where the winners are picked by who is the most devious and ruthless. You want to play them as good guys? Focus on \u201ceveryone gets something out of it\u201d deals, and play up the winners and losers being determined by who is or isn\u2019t willing to put in the effort.<br /> <br /> Primal Ventures are a key point here: invest in a venture that embodies the spirit of the entrepeneur (e.g., innovative and industrious), and you get a dividend in Quintessence \u2014 above and beyond whatever mundane benefits the venture produces on its own. And if those mundane benefits include a monetary profit, well, that\u2019s something you can use to invest in other Primal Ventures. Which means more cash, more Quintessence, and more successful Primal Ventures. That\u2019s such a massive win/win that it would take some serious mismanagement for the Syndicate <i>not</i> to be rolling in resources, both mundane and magical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-21-2013, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T08:11:43-08:00","id":34457,"title":"","content":"So I'm almost done with it (got distracted by The Guild). At this point it seems almost like the Syndicate is objectively Bad, but the individuals, and the individual Methodologies, are pretty <i>good</i>. Only in Mage, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T09:27:55-08:00","id":34474,"title":"","content":"Well, that's the Technocratic Union all over.<br /> <br /> You might want to move onto Void Engineers quickly. Their little piece about a possible Technocratic civil war is highly relevant. The Syndicate are pretty dubious, but they don't really have plans in the way the NWO does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T13:04:51-08:00","id":35088,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">The Syndicate is fighting for a world where everyone can have what they want, even the enemy. You just have to pay for it.<br /> <br /> To the rest of the Technocracy, the Traditions are &quot;superstitionists&quot; -- ignorant fanatics pushing false, self-destructive paradigms and toxic ideologies on innocent sleepers. They're bigoted reactionaries standing in the way of Progress and Enlightenment. They not only want to sabotage humanity's destiny, they want to humanity to turn its back on the notion of Progress entirely. There can be no compromise with such deluded zealots; for the sake of humanity, they and their twisted paradigms must be stamped out. They are the <i>enemy.</i><br /> <br /> The Syndicate, on the other hand, sees the Traditions as <i>untapped markets.</i><br /> <br /> The Syndicate doesn't want you to abandon your existing value system. They want to <i>sell</i> you the things they value. You need ancient grimoires, exotic reagents, sacred relics? Just contact your nearest Syndicate representative. Want to get away from the materialistic corruption of the modern world? The Syndicate can hook you up with meditation retreats, pilgrimage tours, and gated communities where you'll never have to so much as look at anyone who doesn't share your paradigm. Want to convert the sleepers to the One True Way? The Syndicate will set you up with a lucrative publishing contract, a nationwide speaking tour, and your own talk show. These are the guys who invented the <a href=\"http://www.justforhijab.com/2013/11/13/burka-swimsuit-women/\" target=\"_blank\">Burqini;</a> they can monetize <i>anything.</i><br /> <br /> The Syndicate's ideal world isn't a grey, homogeneous dictatorship where all opposing belief systems are prohibited on pain of re-education. It's a rich multicultural tapestry where people of all creeds are free to communicate, socialize, do business, and pursue their own goals in life, without being judged or persecuted. The Syndicate don't want to rule the world. In fact, they're the <i>only</i> faction in Mage that <i>doesn't</i> want to rule the world; the only Convention or Tradition that <i>isn't</i> dominated by ideologues who view even their supposed comrades as &quot;useful idiots.&quot; The Syndicate believes that <i>all</i> paradigms and belief systems have value, and they're eager to leverage that value for everyone's mutual benefit.<br /> <br /> The Syndicate <i>genuinely wants everybody to be friends.</i> They honestly don't understand why everyone else seems to find the idea so horrifying.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/40-dspaul","name":"DSPaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T13:21:29-08:00","id":35093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">The Syndicate <i>genuinely wants everybody to be friends.</i></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Did you read a different book to the one I did?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T14:30:52-08:00","id":35127,"title":"","content":"DSPaul has the basics of it right: the Syndicate prefers cordial relationships to hostilities, as the latter isn\u2019t conducive to good business. They prefer being the suppliers of everyone else\u2019s demands, and aren\u2019t particularly judgmental about the demands that they meet (except to the extent that the nature of the demand influences the price they charge). In many ways, they\u2019re the opposite of the rest of the Technocracy: their dark side tends to take the form of enabling morally dubious behavior and complacency rather than demanding conformity and service. To play them as good guys, you need only pair their \u201cproviding goods and services\u201d mentality with a moral compass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T04:31:30-08:00","id":38674,"title":"","content":"I entirely sympathise with an inherent distrust of the Syndicate, I still have that, but then again. The only CB I read that left a bad taste in my mouth was the NWO, and that's more or less because they creep me out. But, well, the Syndicate...<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the syndicate suffer from a common issue I see in every convention, mistaking the tools for the &quot;magic&quot;. Ironic really because the syndicate will use whatever tools are on hand, they use Int X and Prog Tech, and they're certainly not going to say no to any advances done by the NWO and the Void En, but the key think I took from them is the idea of &quot;value.&quot; There is the common belief that they affect the world by assigning and identifying value, it can be through Quint or through funds, but really what's valuable to a Syndicate member might be utterly esoteric to any other technocrat.<br /> <br /> When I started playing Ascension I challenged myself to create a playable concept for each tradition, when I got the offer to play a technocrat in a big game I had a hard time. I didn't want to play a typical technocrat, so I made a concept that I liked per convention. Ironically the best Syndicate idea I had was not someone who was immediately involved in business, they were a teacher-coach. The idea was to play a person that zeroed in on the people who could change worlds and give them the ability to do so by offering the needed support to succeed. On one hand it could easily be NWO or a Time-Motion manager, but the paradigm was extremely syndicate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1838-danparadox","name":"danparadox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1838_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T08:26:55-08:00","id":40510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danparadox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=38674#post38674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I started playing Ascension I challenged myself to create a playable concept for each tradition....</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very good idea for this game in particular, since a player (or Storyteller) needs to get so far into a character's head to play their approach to magic(k) properly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;</span>Explanations exist; they have existed for all time; there is always a well-known solution to every human problem \u2014 neat, plausible, and wrong.<span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;<br /> - H.L. Mencken</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/467-bob-the-skull","name":"Bob the Skull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T14:20:34-08:00","id":40728,"title":"","content":"I haven't read either Syndicate book, but I once heard someone on a forum suggest that the Syndicate aren't the &quot;1%er&quot; dreamers of amassing huge personal wealth, but more the people who made the dream of making EVERY AMERICAN A HOMEOWNER! a semi-reality in the mid-twentieth century. As has been mentioned elsewhere in this thread, the Syndicate vision (at least at its most optimistic) seems to be the post-scarcity economy.<br /> <br /> It's funny how much more directed the Conventions are than the Traditions. The Trads seem mostly to exist to do whatever idiosyncratic things their individuals value, or maybe to pursue some kind of philosophy; in contrast, the Conventions are wayyy more goal-oriented. Why isn't there a Tradition whose -job- is the fight the Nephandi like the VEs have got? Why isn't there a Tradition whose -job- is to make everybody stronger, better and faster, like the Progenitors? I think that's semi-intentional; the Traditions are fractured by a lack of a shared Paradigm and by rampant individualism generally. In terms of missions, then, in the most abstract, &quot;mystical&quot; sense, it seems like the Syndicate might be on the path to maximize free Quintessence on Earth, so that more and more somethings can be made from nothing. I don't know if that idea is explored within their writeups, but in Mage terms, the road to a post-scarcity economy is paved with Prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1152-crawlkill","name":"crawlkill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T08:31:04-08:00","id":41131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As has been mentioned elsewhere in this thread, the Syndicate vision (at least at its most optimistic) seems to be the post-scarcity economy. </div> </div> </div>Not really. One of their potentially more admirable qualities is that unlike the NWO they don't have big plans for the world, they're happy to maintain the status quo. That doesn't stop them necessarily stating long-term goals, just that it's written to suggest that they don't place great importance on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T08:44:26-08:00","id":41134,"title":"","content":"Oh, it is most assuredly explored! The Syndicate gets a customized variant of Prime called Primal Utility that lets them extract Quintessence from sufficiently innovative and industrious ventures by investing in them. The Syndicate is all about finding people with new ideas and the drive to do something with them and empowering them to do so, which danparadox illustrated nicely in a non-financial way (the ventures they support don\u2019t <i>have</i> to be commercial).<br /> <br /> They\u2019re also about reaping benefits from providing said assistance; they\u2019re not altruists so much as they\u2019re symbiotes \u2014 and, on their bad days, parasites (if they take <i>too much</i> Quintessence from a Primal Venture, they cause it to suffer setbacks). Their failings come in two forms: the more obvious is the temptation to indulge their own wants to the exclusion of others (the so-called one-percenters); the more subtle but equally troubling one is the temptation to cater to peoples\u2019 wants without regard for whether it\u2019s healthy to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T09:16:54-08:00","id":41150,"title":"","content":"One thing I have always been curious about with the syndicate is what does their magic look like? or how would vulgur syndicate magic be like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T09:23:01-08:00","id":41154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=41150#post41150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I have always been curious about with the syndicate is what does their magic look like? or how would vulgur syndicate magic be like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone's bank account going to zero as they're watching their balance on an ATM/online.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T10:09:04-08:00","id":41176,"title":"","content":"The Syndicate does in fact want to be friends with everybody. It's much easier to stab your friends in the back than it is strangers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T10:30:33-08:00","id":41191,"title":"","content":"But there\u2019s also much less <i>reason</i> to stab a friend in the back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T09:14:57-07:00","id":1066359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DSPaul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=35088#post35088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">The Syndicate is fighting for a world where everyone can have what they want, even the enemy. You just have to pay for it.<br /> <br /> To the rest of the Technocracy, the Traditions are &quot;superstitionists&quot; -- ignorant fanatics pushing false, self-destructive paradigms and toxic ideologies on innocent sleepers. They're bigoted reactionaries standing in the way of Progress and Enlightenment. They not only want to sabotage humanity's destiny, they want to humanity to turn its back on the notion of Progress entirely. There can be no compromise with such deluded zealots; for the sake of humanity, they and their twisted paradigms must be stamped out. They are the <i>enemy.</i><br /> <br /> The Syndicate, on the other hand, sees the Traditions as <i>untapped markets.</i><br /> <br /> The Syndicate doesn't want you to abandon your existing value system. They want to <i>sell</i> you the things they value. You need ancient grimoires, exotic reagents, sacred relics? Just contact your nearest Syndicate representative. Want to get away from the materialistic corruption of the modern world? The Syndicate can hook you up with meditation retreats, pilgrimage tours, and gated communities where you'll never have to so much as look at anyone who doesn't share your paradigm. Want to convert the sleepers to the One True Way? The Syndicate will set you up with a lucrative publishing contract, a nationwide speaking tour, and your own talk show. These are the guys who invented the <a href=\"http://www.justforhijab.com/2013/11/13/burka-swimsuit-women/\" target=\"_blank\">Burqini;</a> they can monetize <i>anything.</i><br /> <br /> The Syndicate's ideal world isn't a grey, homogeneous dictatorship where all opposing belief systems are prohibited on pain of re-education. It's a rich multicultural tapestry where people of all creeds are free to communicate, socialize, do business, and pursue their own goals in life, without being judged or persecuted. The Syndicate don't want to rule the world. In fact, they're the <i>only</i> faction in Mage that <i>doesn't</i> want to rule the world; the only Convention or Tradition that <i>isn't</i> dominated by ideologues who view even their supposed comrades as &quot;useful idiots.&quot; The Syndicate believes that <i>all</i> paradigms and belief systems have value, and they're eager to leverage that value for everyone's mutual benefit.<br /> <br /> The Syndicate <i>genuinely wants everybody to be friends.</i> They honestly don't understand why everyone else seems to find the idea so horrifying.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I've started reading the revised CB and I think at their best, they're well-intentioned, but are misguided. I could see a Wall-E type of future where everyone is so used to having their comforts met that they've forgotten what is truly important. The people ended up fat, lazy and with no desire to advance themselves. I know the Syndicate claims that's not what they want, but it could happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T09:30:35-07:00","id":1066372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1066359#post1066359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've started reading the revised CB and I think at their best, they're well-intentioned, but are misguided.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to be dismissive, but &quot;well-intentioned but misguided&quot; can be used to describe pretty much every faction in this game who isn't outright insane.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, it's usually only said of those we personally disagree with. The ones we agree with tend to just be &quot;right&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T10:26:10-07:00","id":1066433,"title":"","content":"True.<br /> <br /> Also, Mages are individuals first and foremost. I don't think that the Syndicate members that profit from drugs or other brands of crime have the most clean or sane morals in the WoD, even if they insist that they're sending individual people to the worst fates imaginable &quot;for the good of the many&quot;.<br /> <br /> Heck, they have a Primal Utility rote that basically it's used to exploit your employes, &quot;slave labor style&quot;, to suck the Quintessence of their bodies. In theory, you can even overwork them to death, if you want (of course, this could be seen as a waste of personel, but still the posibility it's there). This it's not the kind of things that I imagine a &quot;good person&quot; doing, especially when they also could (not mentioned in the book, but can be deduced) give away Quint in order to improve their working force, enhancing their wellfare...<br /> <br /> Then again, I've always felt that good/evil aren't good measures for what mages are and do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T10:55:45-07:00","id":1066459,"title":"","content":"No one is going to do it? Alright.<br /> <br /> Arise, Necro Thread! Arise!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T13:01:40-07:00","id":1066537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1066433#post1066433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True.<br /> <br /> Also, Mages are individuals first and foremost. I don't think that the Syndicate members that profit from drugs or other brands of crime have the most clean or sane morals in the WoD, even if they insist that they're sending individual people to the worst fates imaginable &quot;for the good of the many&quot;.<br /> <br /> Heck, they have a Primal Utility rote that basically it's used to exploit your employes, &quot;slave labor style&quot;, to suck the Quintessence of their bodies. In theory, you can even overwork them to death, if you want (of course, this could be seen as a waste of personel, but still the posibility it's there). This it's not the kind of things that I imagine a &quot;good person&quot; doing, especially when they also could (not mentioned in the book, but can be deduced) give away Quint in order to improve their working force, enhancing their wellfare...<br /> <br /> Then again, I've always felt that good/evil aren't good measures for what mages are and do.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as the Syndicate's model goes, people, as in the mass of Sleepers that generate the Consensus, are, with rare exceptions, completely fungible. Such exceptions do not work in Syndicate sweatshops/Quint farms. Not working your employees to death makes no sense, if working them to death will generate a profit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T19:01:36-07:00","id":1066671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1066537#post1066537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as the Syndicate's model goes, people, as in the mass of Sleepers that generate the Consensus, are, with rare exceptions, completely fungible. Such exceptions do not work in Syndicate sweatshops/Quint farms. Not working your employees to death makes no sense, if working them to death will generate a profit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, but lawsuits, union strikes, and federal investigations have a habit of eating into Profits. As does a high turnover rate of employees broken by the work environment.<br /> <br /> So it's a trade off. There's an upper limit for how much blood can be squeezed from the stone of a business, before the Primal Energy becomes not worth the costs. There's also a general upper limit to how much you can work your employees to death before their productivity plummets. Any responsible (or just practical) Syndicate rep understands this. A given Primal Venture of a given organizational size can only yield so much Quintessence (hence, its &quot;Node&quot; value).<br /> <br /> A irresponsible or impractical Syndicate rep tends to give themselves more trouble for less return.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T14:21:41-07:00","id":1067173,"title":"","content":"Any Syndicate Primal Utility mage who operates a sweatshop who needs to worry about unions or lawsuits or federal investigations needs to be handed over to the Progenitors and broken down for spare parts. Except for the brain as that is apparently something he or she neglected to use. So, on second thought, keep the brain. It might better serve as an advanced abacus or something. Something more useful than what the mage was doing with it. <br /> <br /> The limit doesn't exist because you are still caring about the employees. That is the kind of thinking that gets in the way of profit. It is, in fact, entirely IMpractical. People are replaceable cogs. Work one to death (and there are many many ways to do that that aren't as obvious as it sounds), chain another to the assembly line. That's a great way to reap more Quintessence. <br /> <br /> There is no upper limit (only lack of vision). Pretty much the entire world and most of the history of industrialization proves that hands down (oh and a lot of stuff before then, too, but that I won't lay at the feet of the Syndicate or the High Guild.... though, if they want to own slavery and forced labor then they can have that heaped on their plate as well.) That includes the US where most those things had a brief shining moment before the Syndicate managed to negate or obviate them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T20:49:09-07:00","id":1068534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BC001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=33344#post33344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What\u2019s wrong with the Syndicate is the same thing that is wrong with most of the Technocratic Union in general, namely that it is generally set up as a top-down elitist structure and the ones that make it to the top of that structure tend to be the most driven OCD control freaks in the organization. On top of that, each level they are pressured not to fraternize with those in lower positions for operational security and to avoid influence trickling up the structure from \u201cless informed\u201d levels but it has the side effect of isolating the tiers with each level being \u201cus\u201d to those on it and everyone of lower rank being marginalized and lumped into successively lower levels of \u201cthem\u201d who have less access to information and are theoretically are less competent than those above. Eventually they are reduced to nothing but statistics in the eyes of the higher-ups and no one really cares about the details of numbers, just the bottom line.<br /> <br /> They believe in survival of the fittest, that you have to separate the wheat from the chaff, and all those other cutthroat business adages and to advance in the organization one must be ruthless, efficient, and to put it bluntly cheat and not get caught at it. Some call it unpleasant but necessary expediency for the greater good; others call it criminal disregard for the rules and the rights of others. Personally I see it as more the latter which is why I prefer the Traditions even though they are not without their own glaring flaws.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure I agree with this entirely. The NWO has a lot of conflict with the Syndicate (think about Obamacare/the ACA and how the NWO likely wants socialized/universal healthcare for a variety of noble [elevating/uplifting humanity] and potentially concerning [more control through government] reasons, but the Syndicate likely wants to keep pharmaceutical profits high and permit the free market to remain unregulated so the Syndicate can maximize profits; the Progenitors are likely caught in the middle between huge pharma profits funding their research and their desire to help cure/treat as many people as possible).<br /> <br /> There are certainly similarities among the Conventions of the Technocracy as a whole, but to write them off as a monolith is the conventional Tradition perspective (and likely inaccurate). Believing in &quot;survival of the fittest,&quot; etc. in terms of a free market ideology is very Syndicate, but not necessarily reflective of other conventions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12988-imperator","name":"Imperator","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T03:38:34-07:00","id":1068598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1067173#post1067173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The limit doesn't exist because you are still caring about the employees. That is the kind of thinking that gets in the way of profit. It is, in fact, entirely IMpractical. People are replaceable cogs. Work one to death (and there are many many ways to do that that aren't as obvious as it sounds), chain another to the assembly line. That's a great way to reap more Quintessence.<br /> <br /> There is no upper limit (only lack of vision).</div> </div> </div> </div>While I understand this can get to pretty horrific levels; with a finite population and other groups vying for the parts that you need, I'd say you'd mechanically hit a supply limit at some point. Also, chaining someone to the assembly line through indoctrination and training is not without cost. And then there's the disruption of profits by rebellion and insubordination you'd eventually have to deal with when lower and middle management starts to see upper management as a threat to their personal safety. At some point, it would be like a living creature feeding off itself. You can't do this too much and be strong enough to stand amongst other powerhouses.<br /> <br /> That said, having a number of calculated acceptable losses on the annual ledger is a pretty nasty affair.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T13:32:53-07:00","id":1068837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I understand this can get to pretty horrific levels; with a finite population and other groups vying for the parts that you need, I'd say you'd mechanically hit a supply limit at some point. Also, chaining someone to the assembly line through indoctrination and training is not without cost. And then there's the disruption of profits by rebellion and insubordination you'd eventually have to deal with when lower and middle management starts to see upper management as a threat to their personal safety. At some point, it would be like a living creature feeding off itself. You can't do this too much and be strong enough to stand amongst other powerhouses.<br /> <br /> That said, having a number of calculated acceptable losses on the annual ledger is a pretty nasty affair.</div> </div> </div> </div>This thing varies. Overwork can be found in all parts of the world, and, in some circumstances, it does increase proffit to work people to the death, even in the long run, like in mining (a highly unhealthy profession that doesn't require much capacitation)...Sweat-shops are rather common in many countries, and they ain't going to go away, and they don't cause as much rebelion as one would think. You could also extrapolate the high suicide rate that you find in highly productive and overworked countries,like Japan, and say that an excess of Syndicate greed/influence can produce that effect...Of course, killing highly trained personnel it's not so cheap as killing people that don't need training, but well, the Syndicate has the means to be very aware of how much WORTH has a given individual<br /> <br /> Also, you don't need to indoctrinate people...they indoctrinate themselves willingly, that's the whole point of the system. You need money to be free, thus, you go to work for an amout that it's below the minimun budget if you don't have a lot of choices, and work your life out (quite a paradox, maybe even a Paradox when rebelion does happen). The Syndicate it's based around this, to let people have their own choices, while ensuring that the choices they want to be chosen are better. That's why they're at odds with the NWO (who ARE all about indoctrination)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imperator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure I agree with this entirely. The NWO has a lot of conflict with the Syndicate (think about Obamacare/the ACA and how the NWO likely wants socialized/universal healthcare for a variety of noble [elevating/uplifting humanity] and potentially concerning [more control through government] reasons, but the Syndicate likely wants to keep pharmaceutical profits high and permit the free market to remain unregulated so the Syndicate can maximize profits; the Progenitors are likely caught in the middle between huge pharma profits funding their research and their desire to help cure/treat as many people as possible).<br /> <br /> There are certainly similarities among the Conventions of the Technocracy as a whole, but to write them off as a monolith is the conventional Tradition perspective (and likely inaccurate). Believing in &quot;survival of the fittest,&quot; etc. in terms of a free market ideology is very Syndicate, but not necessarily reflective of other conventions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. The Technos were a bit more of a monolith when Control was in charge, but nowadays they fight with themselves almost as much as the Trads (almost)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-27-2017, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T02:05:14-07:00","id":1069205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1068837#post1068837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This thing varies. Overwork can be found in all parts of the world, and, in some circumstances, it does increase proffit to work people to the death, even in the long run, like in mining (a highly unhealthy profession that doesn't require much capacitation)...Sweat-shops are rather common in many countries, and they ain't going to go away, and they don't cause as much rebelion as one would think. You could also extrapolate the high suicide rate that you find in highly productive and overworked countries,like Japan, and say that an excess of Syndicate greed/influence can produce that effect...Of course, killing highly trained personnel it's not so cheap as killing people that don't need training, but well, the Syndicate has the means to be very aware of how much WORTH has a given individual<br /> <br /> Also, you don't need to indoctrinate people...they indoctrinate themselves willingly, that's the whole point of the system. You need money to be free, thus, you go to work for an amout that it's below the minimun budget if you don't have a lot of choices, and work your life out (quite a paradox, maybe even a Paradox when rebelion does happen). The Syndicate it's based around this, to let people have their own choices, while ensuring that the choices they want to be chosen are better. That's why they're at odds with the NWO (who ARE all about indoctrination)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's true. I was only contesting the statement that there was no upper limit. There is one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T07:31:16-07:00","id":1069337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imperator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1068534#post1068534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are certainly similarities among the Conventions of the Technocracy as a whole, but to write them off as a monolith is the conventional Tradition perspective (and likely inaccurate). Believing in &quot;survival of the fittest,&quot; etc. in terms of a free market ideology is very Syndicate, but not necessarily reflective of other conventions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe social darwinism is an altogether apt comparison for what the Syndicate believes and what they do. Hell, if you read the mid-splat short in the chapter on the Convention's history, it lays out the Syndicate as a Convention believes the root cause of society's ills is the problem of scarcity itself, which is what drives supply and demand, and from that value, wealth, and the power derived from the accumulation and employment of wealth.<br /> <br /> The Syndicate's collective vision of Ascension is the eradication of scarcity itself. When you look at it that way, the Syndicate actually becomes a <b><i>hell</i></b> of a lot more noble than any other Tradition of Convention. How many <i>others</i> have such a self-sacrificial a view of Ascension?<br /> <br /> What I believe is a more fitting statement, is they believe in an idealized Enlightenment (i.e. Adam Smith) view of capitalism and neo-mercantilism wherein a rising tide does, in fact, lift all boats and wealth, over the long term, <i>will</i> distribute itself according to merit opposed to intervening sociopolitics. What they're too hubristic to admit as a Convention, is they're fighting against the weight of millennia of feudalist, dynastic, imperialist, legalist, and absolutist rule, and that the iron rule of oligarchy is too firmly embedded in the Consensus to break in the span of mere centuries; hell, the very concept of international trade as a formal institution is only a development of the 20th Century, for crying out loud.<br /> <br /> The social and political forces surrounding capitalism exert a corrupting force on the latter, not the other way around, and the Syndicate doesn't have an answer to that. Yet, anyways, and assuming the NWO is going to sit back and allow them to implement whatever solution they may find as it would invariably come at heavy price to their own Convention.<br /> <br /> In short, they're Mages. And, they're trapped by their own apparatus and the weight of the Consensus, just like every other Convention. To bring it back to social darwinism, I believe that reflects more the existential morass in which the Syndicate finds itself as it's brought down by the weight of corrupting influence (power-obsessed leadership, losing sight of their goals, combating conflicting goals of other Conventions, Nephandic infiltration, etc.) which plagues every other Convention in its own way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 03-28-2017, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T08:42:15-07:00","id":1069381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe social darwinism is an altogether apt comparison for what the Syndicate believes and what they do. Hell, if you read the mid-splat short in the chapter on the Convention's history, it lays out the Syndicate as a Convention believes the root cause of society's ills is the problem of scarcity itself, which is what drives supply and demand, and from that value, wealth, and the power derived from the accumulation and employment of wealth.<br /> <br /> The Syndicate's collective vision of Ascension is the eradication of scarcity itself. When you look at it that way, the Syndicate actually becomes a <b><i>hell</i></b> of a lot more noble than any other Tradition of Convention. <b>How many <i>others</i> have such a <i>self-sacrificial </i>a view of Ascension</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't get it, why solving the problem of scarcity it's <i>self sacrificial</i>?<br /> <br /> I mean, it sounds good, but remember that this it's the Convention that explicitly doesn't believe in equality (there's an entire rectangle abut that, plus that's why they believe the Craftmasons had to be eradicated).<br /> <br /> <b>They AREN'T about giving up their power and status</b> (if that's what you tought), they just want merit to be the sole factor deciding who it's at the top and who at the bottom (you don't get to be poor because your birth place, but because you're not a gifted individual).<br /> <br /> In other words, they believe that everyone should have the minimal and necessary resources to be able to compete fairly. But only the necessary, everything else it's for the ones who, indeed, are meritory (obviously, they're among the chosen who deserve better).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What I believe is a more fitting statement, is they believe in an idealized Enlightenment (i.e. Adam Smith) view of capitalism and neo-mercantilism wherein a rising tide does, in fact, lift all boats and wealth, over the long term, <i>will</i> distribute itself according to merit opposed to intervening sociopolitics. </div> </div> </div>I agree that the prevalent view it's a top to bottom society where being poor doesn't represent an obstacle to personal progress.<br /> <br /> Having said that, social darwinism it's compatible with that world-view. It's just that competition now it's fair, and thus the &quot;loosers&quot; (in every competition there are loosers) are the ones that &quot;deserve to loose&quot; (because they're not elite enough, they didn't make the effort or just are naturally worse, and not because their education was poor because they were born in the jungle from poor parents). That and social darwinism can be easily married, just cut the ones at the bottom, ensure that the rest has everything they need to prosper (and nothing more). Such a system would need a clear distinction between these, and a good grasp of eugenesics. I can totally see a Syndicate member vouching for the eradication of the problem of scarcity by eradicating the people that aren't productive enough (blaming those who seem to be endemically poor for the scarcity problem, a bit like Malthus).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-28-2017, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T11:45:39-07:00","id":1069511,"title":"","content":"I think the biggest problem with the question of &quot;Is the Syndicate Evil&quot; is the subjective nature of any answer to the question. Evil is a difficult thing to define. Evil denotes profound immorality, wickedness, and depravity... the opposite of &quot;Good&quot;. None of these things are well defined. I doubt there will be general agreement here unless the definition of evil is tackled.<br /> <br /> Does the Syndicate act with the intent of furthering wickedness, depravity, and immorality? I believe the write-ups clearly show that the Syndicate does not act with such interests in mind. They do not see that they do as wicked, depraved, or immoral.<br /> <br /> As per the book, they are committed to establishing the perfect reality of value, pledged to maximizing the worth of the masses' labor, to securing that worth from all forms of devaluation, and to organizing the value structure in accordance with their enlightened leadership and the perception of ultimate power of value among the masses. Their idea of a perfect reality of value is a reality where people earn what they are worth, where people are worth more and more than they used to be, and where the value of each person is protected from devaluation. They eventually want to crate a cashless society in which people can value their potential instead of physical money. In that sense, I think I can safely say that the Syndicate is not founded in evil nor does it have evil ideals. Of course, this does not prove that the Syndicate itself is not evil. Only that it was not meant to be evil.<br /> <br /> So, does the Syndicate perform or promote profound immorality, wickedness, and depravity; wittingly or not? That's where things start to get murky. They support and control the economies of criminal underworlds. Of course, they see this as a necessary thing. They deal with Pentex and some of their members cover up the firms activities. This certainly means they do bad things and that some of their members do evil things. It is noted though that an exposure of their dealings could cause a schism. This would suggest that much of the syndicate isn't evil by virtue of being willing to oppose corruption and wickedness if they were made aware of it. In this sense, I see the Syndicate as being an organization with a peculiar sense of morality that is being tempted and corrupted but as of now is not yet actually evil. The suggestion that a Convention schism could devastate the world economy seems to suggest that they are doing at least some good with regards to keeping the world prosperous, stable, and safe. That's not to say they are awesomely good people. In the end, they're just businessmen. I'd think that if you consider them evil, you'd consider many governments and corporations evil as well.<br /> <br /> Of course, people's sense of evil differ greatly. I'm pretty sure a lot of what I do would be considered evil by someone somewhere. Drawing pictures of people, eating meat, eating certain kinds of meat, not praying to this or that deity, etc. etc.<br /> <br /> On a side note, just to bring it up, it is noted in the Syndicate book that they frown on letting people die of overwork on their jobs and that Un-Enlightened employees are given generous vacations before they crack. This makes sense in that the little bit of profit you would lose by granting a vacation leave is worth far less than the cost of training some new person and of allocating the resources (usually people) to ensure that a new person fits in to a certain post. It's better to preserve someone who is certain to be productive and is further along the path to being even more productive. Liabilities to the Syndicate would not likely be willing to work themselves to death for the good of the Syndicate. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T17:12:45-07:00","id":1069727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1068598#post1068598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I understand this can get to pretty horrific levels; with a finite population and other groups vying for the parts that you need, I'd say you'd mechanically hit a supply limit at some point. Also, chaining someone to the assembly line through indoctrination and training is not without cost. And then there's the disruption of profits by rebellion and insubordination you'd eventually have to deal with when lower and middle management starts to see upper management as a threat to their personal safety. At some point, it would be like a living creature feeding off itself. You can't do this too much and be strong enough to stand amongst other powerhouses.<br /> <br /> That said, having a number of calculated acceptable losses on the annual ledger is a pretty nasty affair.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Those are rose-colored glasses you're wearing. The human population vis-av-vis the Syndicate's use of them in Primal Utility sweatshops is infinite. That's the easily disposable, not going to be missed fraction of the human population, which is a hefty percentage of 7 billion people. You CAN do that effectively forever.<br /> <br /> The inherent problem with the Syndicate's paradigm of Hypercapitalism is that, in pretty much every way, it is a race to the moral bottom. If you can make a profit by doing these sorts of things, you then you have to or you will be replaced by someone who will. You ARE asnwerable to the Stockholders. They demand PROFIT, not excuses about why you decided NOT to make it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T20:19:22-07:00","id":1069817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1069727#post1069727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those are rose-colored glasses you're wearing. The human population vis-av-vis the Syndicate's use of them in Primal Utility sweatshops is infinite. That's the easily disposable, not going to be missed fraction of the human population, which is a hefty percentage of 7 billion people. You CAN do that effectively forever.<br /> <br /> The inherent problem with the Syndicate's paradigm of Hypercapitalism is that, in pretty much every way, it is a race to the moral bottom. If you can make a profit by doing these sorts of things, you then you have to or you will be replaced by someone who will. You ARE asnwerable to the Stockholders. They demand PROFIT, not excuses about why you decided NOT to make it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rose colored glasses? I didn't say it was a low limit or that limit put them on the side of good. I simply said there was a mechanical limit. Obviously, they cannot kill more than the human population. Nor can they kill more than their organizational population. They could not kill more people than they could bring into their program each day without serious problems. When I say limit, I only mean they can only kill X number of people a day (or per recruitment period, whatever that is). That's all. This is not an infinite number because the number of people killed per time period can be recorded and there is a maximum number to how many people can be killed. A projection can be made for how many people they can possibly kill this way per year.<br /> <br /> And as noted in a certain part of the Syndicate book, they don't even like overworking their employees to death. It is wasteful. They have a rote developed just so they don't need to overwork people to death. This isn't even them being nice. The people can be saved from death and used for quintessence again later with minimal disruption to operations. The people are also used for something other than quintessence and that other thing also has value, otherwise you'd have something more like the iteration X prison planet (which they would think is a gross mismanagement of resources) or human sacrifice quintessence converters (Which maybe they tried during WW2).<br /> <br /> I think they've found that killing people adds to the cost of the production of quintessence.<br /> <br /> Also, a thorough reading of them has led me to see that they are not actually after profit. They do not answer to shareholders in the same sense that a normal company does. They want control of the flow of resources to use as a tool to control the masses and herd them towards the goal of their vision of ascension. They do not want profit for profit's sake because at a certain point, it means nothing to them. They aren't even hypercapitalist. Capitalism is merely a tool for them and they use it because it is what people believe in right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 03-29-2017, 04:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T05:34:31-07:00","id":1069992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1069727#post1069727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those are rose-colored glasses you're wearing. The human population vis-av-vis the Syndicate's use of them in Primal Utility sweatshops is infinite. That's the easily disposable, not going to be missed fraction of the human population, which is a hefty percentage of 7 billion people. You CAN do that effectively forever.<br /> <br /> The inherent problem with the Syndicate's paradigm of Hypercapitalism is that, in pretty much every way, it is a race to the moral bottom. If you can make a profit by doing these sorts of things, you then you have to or you will be replaced by someone who will. You ARE asnwerable to the Stockholders. They demand PROFIT, not excuses about why you decided NOT to make it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see this as a good description of a way a Syndicate agent might get sidelined and trapped by his own paradigm. One of the pitfalls, say, and not the standard state of affairs. In general, though, they are not interested in humans because of money, they are interested in money because of humans. The Syndicate is all about leveraging potential and there is no greater potential in their eyes than humanity. Profit is only one representation of that potential, often not even the best one. <br /> <br /> As far as the Syndicate is concerned, all of the greatest cultural and technological works have been produced by wealthy societies. The more people they can free up to do those great works the higher humanity can stand. One day no one will have to work towards supporting themselves or anyone else and every drop of effort can but put into leisure and worthy pursuits. Humanity will be free to rise beyond limit.<br /> <br /> And if that means ruthlessly exploiting people in the here and now, so be it. Anything is worth that utopian dream.<br /> <br /> Hey, I never said these guys were moral.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T07:58:23-07:00","id":1070068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BC001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=33344#post33344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What\u2019s wrong with the Syndicate is the same thing that is wrong with most of the Technocratic Union in general, namely that it is generally set up as a top-down elitist structure and the ones that make it to the top of that structure tend to be the most driven OCD control freaks in the organization. On top of that, each level they are pressured not to fraternize with those in lower positions for operational security and to avoid influence trickling up the structure from \u201cless informed\u201d levels but it has the side effect of isolating the tiers with each level being \u201cus\u201d to those on it and everyone of lower rank being marginalized and lumped into successively lower levels of \u201cthem\u201d who have less access to information and are theoretically are less competent than those above. Eventually they are reduced to nothing but statistics in the eyes of the higher-ups and no one really cares about the details of numbers, just the bottom line.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This^<br /> <br /> The Technocracy is rife with the same systemic corruption that perverts our democracy. Humans have a pyramid of people they care about. They care about themselves and their children the most, then their friends, then people with the same sub-culture as themselves. Past that they may care for bigger groups a little, but not enough that it will consistently motivate their behavior. To mitigate this, the most successful systems need heavy transparency, and heavy checks and balances. Via heavy transparency, the human tendency to only care deeply and consistently about a small group of people is mitigated by everyone in power feeling the eyes of the people they lead upon them. It's also why the countries with the highest happiness index are socialist rather than communist or capitalist. Communism creates a bureaucratic oligarchy infested with a lack of transparency and checks and balances, and has them rule over people who are more motivated to game the system than they are to work hard. Capitalism creates an oligarchy of the rich who control politicians via campaign donations, create quasi-monopolies, and exploit the poorest workers the hardest. Both systems fail because they do not have mechanisms to mitigate and channel human nature. Places like Norway have heavy political mechanisms to mitigate and channel the flaws in human nature, and hey look at that they also have the highest reported happiness index by far.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T08:52:52-07:00","id":1070121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1070068#post1070068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This^<br /> <br /> The Technocracy is rife with the same systemic corruption that perverts our democracy. Humans have a pyramid of people they care about. They care about themselves and their children the most, then their friends, then people with the same sub-culture as themselves. Past that they may care for bigger groups a little, but not enough that it will consistently motivate their behavior. To mitigate this, the most successful systems need heavy transparency, and heavy checks and balances. Via heavy transparency, the human tendency to only care deeply and consistently about a small group of people is mitigated by everyone in power feeling the eyes of the people they lead upon them. It's also why the countries with the highest happiness index are socialist rather than communist or capitalist. Communism creates a bureaucratic oligarchy infested with a lack of transparency and checks and balances, and has them rule over people who are more motivated to game the system than they are to work hard. Capitalism creates an oligarchy of the rich who control politicians via campaign donations, create quasi-monopolies, and exploit the poorest workers the hardest. Both systems fail because they do not have mechanisms to mitigate and channel human nature. Places like Norway have heavy political mechanisms to mitigate and channel the flaws in human nature, and hey look at that they also have the highest reported happiness index by far.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think you just expressed the NWO party line. Especially the 'flaws in human nature' part. Did a manila envelope make it's way under your door last night? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T08:53:52-07:00","id":1070122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1070068#post1070068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also why the countries with the highest happiness index are socialist rather than communist or capitalist.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1070068#post1070068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Places like Norway have heavy political mechanisms to mitigate and channel the flaws in human nature, and hey look at that they also have the highest reported happiness index by far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, didn't the prime minister of Denmark say that the Nordic model is not a socialist planned economy but a market economy? Could you define what you mean by socialism in this sense?<br /> <br /> What I understand of the way things are run over there is that everyone has free education and universal healthcare, representatives of labor and employers negotiate wages and labor market policy mediated by the government, and private ownership, free markets and free trade are encouraged. I don't quite see where socialism fits in exactly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T09:09:43-07:00","id":1070133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1069992#post1069992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see this as a good description of a way a Syndicate agent might get sidelined and trapped by his own paradigm. One of the pitfalls, say, and not the standard state of affairs. In general, though, they are not interested in humans because of money, they are interested in money because of humans. The Syndicate is all about leveraging potential and there is no greater potential in their eyes than humanity. Profit is only one representation of that potential, often not even the best one.<br /> <br /> As far as the Syndicate is concerned, all of the greatest cultural and technological works have been produced by wealthy societies. The more people they can free up to do those great works the higher humanity can stand. One day no one will have to work towards supporting themselves or anyone else and every drop of effort can but put into leisure and worthy pursuits. Humanity will be free to rise beyond limit.<br /> <br /> And if that means ruthlessly exploiting people in the here and now, so be it. Anything is worth that utopian dream.<br /> <br /> Hey, I never said these guys were moral.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In a rancher's eye, there is no greater value for cattle than beef.<br /> <br /> Screw Utopia, I have to up my profit margins EVERY QUARTER or get &quot;downsized&quot; into a role more &quot;fitting to my abilities&quot;.<br /> <br /> Screw them now, screw them later. The problem with the Syndicate paradigm is and pretty much always has been that it really isn't about &quot;Value&quot; except in an idealized and debased sense. Idealized in that it's not really about making things better for those for who things should be better. Debased in that expressed value is really about about showing that you're one of those blessed. The Syndicate's sin is Greed. It's fundamentally tainted everything they do and everything they've planned to do. They aren't concerned about &quot;tomorrow&quot; when there's a bottom line TODAY. <br /> <br /> Sure, you can play some dewy-eyed waif which a degree in economics that thinks that they are going to make the world a better place, but the innocence or the person will CRASH into the reality the Syndicate has constructed and to pretty much every possible degree of evaluation, is entirely happy with, absent some propganda to the contrary. <br /> <br /> (BTW, I'm not hating on the Synicate especially. I can do this for pretty much every Sect. But the Syndicate makes it sooooooooo easy. It's gotta be impossible for them to believe the crap they peddle when they are the expert peddlers. There's a reason why the Technephandi seem to be most grounded in the High Guild/Syndicate. Same for the SPD. The Syndicate is the kind of organization that finds out it has a cold than thinks that the solution is infecting itself with anthrax.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T10:05:59-07:00","id":1070174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1070133#post1070133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Screw Utopia, I have to up my profit margins EVERY QUARTER or get &quot;downsized&quot; into a role more &quot;fitting to my abilities&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why does everyone seem to think the Syndicate has to up the profit margin ad infinitum? The Syndicate Board doesn't have shareholders to answer to and their goal is a perfect global economy of cashless trade &quot;in which people can value their potential instead of physical money&quot;. This won't happen if they gather resources at an unsustainable rate, hoard those resources, and then put these in a box somewhere. To them it's just influence, magick, and numbers. They know that making money is &quot;ultimately a form of Myopia&quot; and that the power of money comes only from the shared belief in the power of money. They have to use this wealth at some point for it to be worth anything. Syndicate Chairmen (people, one rank below the Board) are expected to have overcome their greed or they are terminated. They are not expected to fill their coffers for the sake of filling their coffers. They are expected to get things done. It's just that what they do costs money, lots of money, but not so much money that they cannot eventually have the money they need to get their part of the job done or find a cheaper alternative. Saying &quot;Screw Utopia&quot; is what gets you taken away by the Syndicate Enforcers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1070133#post1070133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They aren't concerned about &quot;tomorrow&quot; when there's a bottom line TODAY.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their book makes them out to be quite concerned about tomorrow.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that these guys are good guys. Heck, they don't really expect the masses to Ascend and are simply placing themselves in the position to control Ascension. I'm just saying that the above lines of argument seem to contradict what they are.<br /> <br /> What I'd consider their bad points are:<br /> The absolutely ruthless way they use their influence in their attempts to achieve their goals.<br /> How they attempt to be in control of everyone and everything.<br /> Pentex<br /> Their crime connections<br /> Their tendency towards an end justifies the means philosophy<br /> Stuff like that<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 03-30-2017, 06:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T21:47:36-07:00","id":1070482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1070174#post1070174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why does everyone seem to think the Syndicate has to up the profit margin ad infinitum? The Syndicate Board doesn't have shareholders to answer to and their goal is a perfect global economy of cashless trade &quot;in which people can value their potential instead of physical money&quot;. This won't happen if they gather resources at an unsustainable rate, hoard those resources, and then put these in a box somewhere. To them it's just influence, magick, and numbers. They know that making money is &quot;ultimately a form of Myopia&quot; and that the power of money comes only from the shared belief in the power of money. They have to use this wealth at some point for it to be worth anything. Syndicate Chairmen (people, one rank below the Board) are expected to have overcome their greed or they are terminated. They are not expected to fill their coffers for the sake of filling their coffers. They are expected to get things done. It's just that what they do costs money, lots of money, but not so much money that they cannot eventually have the money they need to get their part of the job done or find a cheaper alternative. Saying &quot;Screw Utopia&quot; is what gets you taken away by the Syndicate Enforcers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. The Syndicate upper ranks see the pursuit of profit the same way Traditionalists see great magical might: useful as far as it goes, but ultimately a distraction. Contrary to the message the Syndicate fosters among the uneducated masses, Money does not, itself, have value. Money is only valuable for the things it can buy. The Convention has seen currency of all kinds fail and markets implode too many times to truly trust money. Why do you think they seek a cashless society?<br /> <br /> Naturally, the reality of the Syndicate is a mix of Pure Profiteering and Utopian Ideal. Just as Hermetics can and do fall for the trap of hubris, so too do many Syndicate reps fall to the temptation of greed. It's a persistent problem that causes debacles like the Special Projects Division to form, in service of innovation at the lowest bidder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T07:01:14-07:00","id":1070614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. The Syndicate upper ranks see the pursuit of profit the same way Traditionalists see great magical might: useful as far as it goes, but ultimately a distraction. Contrary to the message the Syndicate fosters among the uneducated masses, Money does not, itself, have value. Money is only valuable for the things it can buy. The Convention has seen currency of all kinds fail and markets implode too many times to truly trust money. Why do you think they seek a cashless society?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but if &quot;The Syndicate upper ranks see the pursuit of profit the same way Traditionalists see great magical might&quot;, then we're doomed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> , because high ranking Traditionalists usually are very, VERY, much in love with their magical might...<b>Porthos wasn't</b>, but he was an exeption, most cabals of Masters, or even Archmasters, think highly about power.<br /> <br /> Now, if my memory doesn't fail, the Syndicate oldest master (and founder) <b>Wolfgang von Reismann</b> was very much in love with his power. More to the point, he was able to do anything for the promise of immortality. He's supposed to be dead now (or maybe in the body of his sucessor?. Well, he was lost to the Storm, or wasn't he?), but I find hard to believe that every, or even most, of the upper echelons of the $indicate are so pure of heart as their book want's to pressent them.<br /> <br /> In Mage, Old Masters aren't usually examples of morality...In Mage the motto &quot;power corrupts&quot; it's very much a thing, and more often than not, those who live enough to reach to these powerful places aren't so &quot;(Human)-ist&quot; anymore. If they're like the Traditions in any way, I'm sure that there are some trully devout Utopian in the &quot;upper ranks&quot;, and perhaps these are the most powerful members of the lot (Hey, Phortos was no pushover) but probably most aren't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-30-2017, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T08:17:10-07:00","id":1070648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1070614#post1070614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, but if &quot;The Syndicate upper ranks see the pursuit of profit the same way Traditionalists see great magical might&quot;, then we're doomed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> , because high ranking Traditionalists usually are very, VERY, much in love with their magical might...<b>Porthos wasn't</b>, but he was an exeption, most cabals of Masters, or even Archmasters, think highly about power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that doesn't seem to be quite right.<br /> Actually, tradition mages tend to see greater and greater magical might as a great part of their self worth.<br /> While Syndicate mages can also see profit as a measure of self worth, they are told to remember that profit is just a tool to control the masses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1070614#post1070614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, if my memory doesn't fail, the Syndicate oldest master (and founder) <b>Wolfgang von Reismann</b> was very much in love with his power. More to the point, he was able to do anything for the promise of immortality. He's supposed to be dead now (or maybe in the body of his sucessor?. Well, he was lost to the Storm, or wasn't he?), but I find hard to believe that every, or even most, of the upper echelons of the $indicate are so pure of heart as their book want's to pressent them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pure of heart? Hardly. In their ideal world, those with greatest value will be given the most reward. Sounds altruistic but with the way they work, it means that they want to recruit those of greatest value to their number so that those of greatest value will still always be the upper echelon of the Syndicate. Furthermore, their vision of a cashless society that they control will actually lead to them pretty much having even more control over reality than they currently do. There's nothing altruistic about it. Instead of Ascension for All, they plan to Ascend before anyone else by creating a reality where the Syndicate controls each person's reality... mainly because they see the masses as incapable of making decent decisions and they feel that everyone else is blind to what they see as the easy path to Ascension for those who are worthy. &quot;Everyone living in a land of plenty&quot; is merely what they expect to be the happy side-effect of their rise to power.<br /> <br /> My main concern is that people seem to equate profit with the Syndicate's main goal. The main goal of the Syndicate is power, not profit. Money is meant to be spent and used as leverage to gain power, and not hoarded. They want to control the flow of money. For that to happen, money has to flow.<br /> <br /> As for their being evil, I personally see them as terribly pragmatic rather than evil, but evil is a very relative term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T09:17:12-07:00","id":1070689,"title":"","content":"They also tend to confuse the model for the people. Economic systems may be human systems, but economics are not human. The Syndicate is unabashedly human-centric in theory, but it often loses sight of the faces that make up humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T14:15:04-07:00","id":1070853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1070174#post1070174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why does everyone seem to think the Syndicate has to up the profit margin ad infinitum? The Syndicate Board doesn't have shareholders to answer to and their goal is a perfect global economy of cashless trade &quot;in which people can value their potential instead of physical money&quot;. This won't happen if they gather resources at an unsustainable rate, hoard those resources, and then put these in a box somewhere. To them it's just influence, magick, and numbers. They know that making money is &quot;ultimately a form of Myopia&quot; and that the power of money comes only from the shared belief in the power of money. They have to use this wealth at some point for it to be worth anything. Syndicate Chairmen (people, one rank below the Board) are expected to have overcome their greed or they are terminated. They are not expected to fill their coffers for the sake of filling their coffers. They are expected to get things done. It's just that what they do costs money, lots of money, but not so much money that they cannot eventually have the money they need to get their part of the job done or find a cheaper alternative. Saying &quot;Screw Utopia&quot; is what gets you taken away by the Syndicate Enforcers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Their book makes them out to be quite concerned about tomorrow.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that these guys are good guys. Heck, they don't really expect the masses to Ascend and are simply placing themselves in the position to control Ascension. I'm just saying that the above lines of argument seem to contradict what they are.<br /> <br /> What I'd consider their bad points are:<br /> The absolutely ruthless way they use their influence in their attempts to achieve their goals.<br /> How they attempt to be in control of everyone and everything.<br /> Pentex<br /> Their crime connections<br /> Their tendency towards an end justifies the means philosophy<br /> Stuff like that<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Their book is pretty much the best job of self-aggrandizing white-washing possible. Which makes sense since that's EXACTLY what they are and what they do. They Syndicate in the Syndicate's eyes is the be-all-end-all of the Union, saviors of the World through CAPITALISM (to end up with a post-scarcity society... err... that makes no sense...... Stop thinking and JUST WATCH THE VIDEO... It will explain everything....)<br /> <br /> Actions speak louder than words. <br /> <br /> You don't NEED to be ruthless to achieve those goals. At all. In fact, being ruthless is absolutely counter-productive to achieving those goals. If they are being ruthless (and that's a very polite way to put the actions that have been described as Syndicate SOP), those aren't their goals. And that makes since, since, like every other group of powerful humans ever, the Syndicate's No. 1 priority is the advancement of the Syndicate. If you take these rose-colored glasses, here, and put them on, like this.... Then they HAVE to do that or else they WON'T be ABLE to MAKE the world WONDERFUL for Humanity!!!!!! And cashless and no one will feel bad and there will be rainbows!!!!!!!<br /> <br /> You don't need to be in control of everyone and everything. See above, plus, if you even TRY this you are hip deep in moral quicksand and alligators.<br /> <br /> Yes. Pentex. And SPD. And the Technephandi. And just being douchey running drug cartels, top down finance big business, being the origin and nexus of all false advertising... and, oh yeah, running those Primal Utility sweatshop assembly lines. <br /> <br /> The Synidicate is in crime is because crime is where the profit is. If their (possibly) laudable goals were actually their goals at all, they would be work against crime functionally and conceptually, as it is working outside the system they are espousing as the mainline to Nirvana. But they don't. Because the Syndicate WANTS there to be crime (and the quasi-criminal) to be the norm. That's not a bug, that's a feature. <br /> <br /> See &quot;moral quicksand and alligators&quot; above with regard to ends justify the means. (Which is the Union's Cardinal Sin as a whole... Pride.... WE know best. WE have the right way. And it's the reason that, if you like the Technephandi, and I know the writes LOVE them, the Technephandi got their foot in the door, across the room, a seat at the table and slipped everyone else a mickey in their drinks...) <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T14:47:47-07:00","id":1070865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1070853#post1070853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See &quot;moral quicksand and alligators&quot; above with regard to ends justify the means. (Which is the Union's Cardinal Sin as a whole... Pride.... WE know best. WE have the right way. And it's the reason that, if you like the Technephandi, and I know the writes LOVE them, the Technephandi got their foot in the door, across the room, a seat at the table and slipped everyone else a mickey in their drinks...)</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, Iteration X has their ducks in a row as far as 'this is the future we want' and 'this is what we're doing'. Of course their ideology could be considered Darwinism at best, and psychotic perfectionism at worst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T17:25:39-07:00","id":1070945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1070865#post1070865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, Iteration X has their ducks in a row as far as 'this is the future we want' and 'this is what we're doing'. Of course their ideology could be considered Darwinism at best, and psychotic perfectionism at worst.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least they aren't hypocrites. Nor are they snake-oil salesman with a bill of goods that makes them appear to be hypocrites when they are actually aren't, they're just sociopathic user spin doctors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T18:30:53-07:00","id":1070965,"title":"","content":"The syndicate only want a nice world because they live in it and want to save the world in the sense of keeping it intact as much as possible because they eventually intend to control it. As mentioned in the book, they are positioning themselves for ascension (They believe once they control reality, they will ascend), not proposing an Ascension for the masses. They want a post scarcity society because they want to live in a reality where they themselves don't have to worry about scarcity. Amusingly, I their vision of a the ideal world is a bit saner than what some of the other Conventions propose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1070853#post1070853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Their book is pretty much the best job of self-aggrandizing white-washing possible. Which makes sense since that's EXACTLY what they are and what they do. They Syndicate in the Syndicate's eyes is the be-all-end-all of the Union, saviors of the World through CAPITALISM (to end up with a post-scarcity society... err... that makes no sense...... Stop thinking and JUST WATCH THE VIDEO... It will explain everything....)</div> </div> </div> </div>Capitalism is a tool they intend to discard at some point.<br /> <br /> If you want something like a plan outline, it would be something like:<br /> Control the world economy<br /> Gain fine control over the finances of the masses<br /> Use control over the masses to control the belief of the masses<br /> Use the belief of the masses as a tool to solve problems and make the economy of their dreams<br /> Their plan is pretty vague past this point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1070853#post1070853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't NEED to be ruthless to achieve those goals. At all. In fact, being ruthless is absolutely counter-productive to achieving those goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>How exactly are you going to gain control of the world and be the first to &quot;Ascension&quot; without being ruthless? They might even eventually have to shut down the other convention's Ascension ideas at some point. What actually do you think are their goals?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1070853#post1070853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... and, oh yeah, running those Primal Utility sweatshop assembly lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, where is there mention of these sweatshops? I'm kinda looking for them in the book now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1070853#post1070853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Synidicate is in crime is because crime is where the profit is. If their (possibly) laudable goals were actually their goals at all, they would be work against crime functionally and conceptually, as it is working outside the system they are espousing as the mainline to Nirvana. But they don't. Because the Syndicate WANTS there to be crime (and the quasi-criminal) to be the norm. That's not a bug, that's a feature.</div> </div> </div> </div>They want in on crime, particularly vice crime, because it's an easy way to gain control of people. What sort of system are they espousing exactly?<br /> <br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong. I don't see these guys as any better than the other conventions but I don't quite see some of the points you are trying to make.<br /> <br /> (also, I enjoy friendly healthy debate)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T19:06:08-07:00","id":1070983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1070965#post1070965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How exactly are you going to gain control of the world and be the first to &quot;Ascension&quot; without being ruthless? They might even eventually have to shut down the other convention's Ascension ideas at some point. What actually do you think are their goals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this is Mage, so you would just need to have a Total Caring Paradigm, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T23:19:33-07:00","id":1071089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1070983#post1070983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, this is Mage, so you would just need to have a Total Caring Paradigm, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Carebear Countdown as a focus for for Mind!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T08:02:41-07:00","id":1071258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1066433#post1066433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True.<br /> <br /> Also, Mages are individuals first and foremost. I don't think that the Syndicate members that profit from drugs or other brands of crime have the most clean or sane morals in the WoD, even if they insist that they're sending individual people to the worst fates imaginable &amp;quot;for the good of the many&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Heck, they have a Primal Utility rote that basically it's used to exploit your employes, &amp;quot;slave labor style&amp;quot;, to suck the Quintessence of their bodies. In theory, you can even overwork them to death, if you want (of course, this could be seen as a waste of personel, but still the posibility it's there). This it's not the kind of things that I imagine a &amp;quot;good person&amp;quot; doing, especially when they also could (not mentioned in the book, but can be deduced) give away Quint in order to improve their working force, enhancing their wellfare...<br /> <br /> Then again, I've always felt that good/evil aren't good measures for what mages are and do.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the Prime 3 Rotes for Chorus and Verbena has human/animal sacrifice. A rote is an application, not a display of the ideals of the group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11894-shushu","name":"Shushu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T10:45:42-07:00","id":1071320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1070965#post1070965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The syndicate only want a nice world because they live in it and want to save the world in the sense of keeping it intact as much as possible because they eventually intend to control it. As mentioned in the book, they are positioning themselves for ascension (They believe once they control reality, they will ascend), not proposing an Ascension for the masses. They want a post scarcity society because they want to live in a reality where they themselves don't have to worry about scarcity. Amusingly, I their vision of a the ideal world is a bit saner than what some of the other Conventions propose.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Capitalism is a tool they intend to discard at some point.<br /> <br /> If you want something like a plan outline, it would be something like:<br /> Control the world economy<br /> Gain fine control over the finances of the masses<br /> Use control over the masses to control the belief of the masses<br /> Use the belief of the masses as a tool to solve problems and make the economy of their dreams<br /> Their plan is pretty vague past this point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> How exactly are you going to gain control of the world and be the first to &quot;Ascension&quot; without being ruthless? They might even eventually have to shut down the other convention's Ascension ideas at some point. What actually do you think are their goals?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, where is there mention of these sweatshops? I'm kinda looking for them in the book now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They want in on crime, particularly vice crime, because it's an easy way to gain control of people. What sort of system are they espousing exactly?<br /> <br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong. I don't see these guys as any better than the other conventions but I don't quite see some of the points you are trying to make.<br /> <br /> (also, I enjoy friendly healthy debate)<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Syndicate doesn't seem to care about living in a nice world at all. At least outside of a nice world for members of the Syndicate and those currently useful to the Syndicate. They get to live in a very very nice world indeed. In fact, they live in a something of a post-scarcity meritocracy as they can provide for all their wants and needs, and what they can't simply provides motivation to prove oneself.. Especially when all the other Conventions are put in their place as functional units of the Syndicate-as-Union or are properly disposed of as unecessary. (And, yes, that is a very definite end goal as the Syndicate's current structure and goals are set forth). Ascension is just mouthing the relevant dogma. I don't think most Syndicate personnel give it two shakes unless they need to use it for in-Union spin. Ascension is pretty much a cipher in Mage that stands for &quot;what we say we want&quot; but that no one really seems to. Pretty much no organization or individual depicted has any real desire to spend time or effort to achieve it. <br /> <br /> Is capitalism a tool they intend to discard at some point? They seem awfully invested in it. As in, shoving it down the world's collective throat since before the High Guild showed up for that first meeting of the Order of Reason, on through all that imperialism and down to the present where they have managed to successfully capitalize every alternative method of resource allocation that anyone else has come up with. Oh, and take credit for coming up with it as they bowdlerize it to make it function withing the constraints of the profit motive. <br /> <br /> How do you take control of the world without being ruthless? The answer is implicit in the question. By not being ruthless. By not supporting endeavors that victimize people and move things further and further away from your purported goals (such as, I dunno, CRIME). By using your powers of persuasion and creation of value in a positive manner. In really promoting a post-scarcity economy in an egalitarian meritocratic society (which means playing nice with NWO instead of trying to undermine them to the point of irrelevance... which won't work really, economy and governments are inextricably intertwined at a fundamental level that exists at all levels of human society) But that would entail some really selfless beneficent thinking and, the proof isn't in the pudding, it's in the eating. They AREN'T selfless, they are the very benchmark of greedy. They AREN'T beneficent, they are the very definition of selfish. <br /> <br /> &quot;Sweatshops&quot; aren't called that per se, but they are implicit in the descriptions of the ways that Primal Utility can be used. Particularly in the Syndicate book. Sure you COULD invest in a wonderful little start-up that makes an ap that creates joy or work with the VE to create shipyards for new Voidships that could become partially self-sustaining feedback loops where the Quint harvested could go into the Device creation, but that's not what ends up happening if you want to show the boss that you can add to the Syndicate's Quint stockpiles and invest in their ability to keep the power of the purse going strong and keep a tight rein on the other Conventions. <br /> <br /> They aren't worse that the other Conventions in action. Well, maybe a little, as the effects of their perfidy are felt more than, say, the Progenitors and It-X, which are probably just as cruel, but it tends to be less broadcast to the population as a whole. And maybe a little more than the NWO, though that is a close one. But the emphasis on competition probably puts them a little more to the black than the NWO and it's push for conformity. Everyone is worse than the Void Engineers. <br /> <br /> That plan is about as coherent as that of the underwear gnomes in South Park. And seems vague enough to make one think of selling hamburgers with nearly naked women in swimsuits or cars perched on top of mesas that no car could get to without being lowered by a helicopter. Meaning, welcome to our hype and thank you for buying it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T11:30:40-07:00","id":1071342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1071320#post1071320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Syndicate doesn't seem to care about living in a nice world at all. At least outside of a nice world for members of the Syndicate and those currently useful to the Syndicate. They get to live in a very very nice world indeed. In fact, they live in a something of a post-scarcity meritocracy as they can provide for all their wants and needs, and what they can't simply provides motivation to prove oneself.. Especially when all the other Conventions are put in their place as functional units of the Syndicate-as-Union or are properly disposed of as unecessary. (And, yes, that is a very definite end goal as the Syndicate's current structure and goals are set forth). Ascension is just mouthing the relevant dogma. I don't think most Syndicate personnel give it two shakes unless they need to use it for in-Union spin. Ascension is pretty much a cipher in Mage that stands for &quot;what we say we want&quot; but that no one really seems to. Pretty much no organization or individual depicted has any real desire to spend time or effort to achieve it.<br /> <br /> Is capitalism a tool they intend to discard at some point? They seem awfully invested in it. As in, shoving it down the world's collective throat since before the High Guild showed up for that first meeting of the Order of Reason, on through all that imperialism and down to the present where they have managed to successfully capitalize every alternative method of resource allocation that anyone else has come up with. Oh, and take credit for coming up with it as they bowdlerize it to make it function withing the constraints of the profit motive.<br /> <br /> How do you take control of the world without being ruthless? The answer is implicit in the question. By not being ruthless. By not supporting endeavors that victimize people and move things further and further away from your purported goals (such as, I dunno, CRIME). By using your powers of persuasion and creation of value in a positive manner. In really promoting a post-scarcity economy in an egalitarian meritocratic society (which means playing nice with NWO instead of trying to undermine them to the point of irrelevance... which won't work really, economy and governments are inextricably intertwined at a fundamental level that exists at all levels of human society) But that would entail some really selfless beneficent thinking and, the proof isn't in the pudding, it's in the eating. They AREN'T selfless, they are the very benchmark of greedy. They AREN'T beneficent, they are the very definition of selfish.<br /> <br /> &quot;Sweatshops&quot; aren't called that per se, but they are implicit in the descriptions of the ways that Primal Utility can be used. Particularly in the Syndicate book. Sure you COULD invest in a wonderful little start-up that makes an ap that creates joy or work with the VE to create shipyards for new Voidships that could become partially self-sustaining feedback loops where the Quint harvested could go into the Device creation, but that's not what ends up happening if you want to show the boss that you can add to the Syndicate's Quint stockpiles and invest in their ability to keep the power of the purse going strong and keep a tight rein on the other Conventions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most faction plans only make sense from an in Paradigm perspective, Mage is remarkably Kuhnian that way. There are all sorts of things that only make sense because believers just wouldn't think to act a different way, or ask the dangerous questions, etc. The Syndicate has all sorts of checks and balances that aren't obvious to outsiders that keep things from getting out of hand. They also have failings that aren't obvious to their members. <br /> <br /> And I have to say, from my perspective, the Syndicate is actually remarkably easy to depict as a well-meaning and often positive force. They definitely have failings, many of which have already been listed, but they actually value human achievement in a way most of the rest of the Technocracy doesn't. If I had to chose between the Syndicate and the NWO it would be the Syndicate any day of the week.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T12:33:28-07:00","id":1071371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1071320#post1071320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Syndicate doesn't seem to care about living in a nice world at all. At least outside of a nice world for members of the Syndicate and those currently useful to the Syndicate. They get to live in a very very nice world indeed. In fact, they live in a something of a post-scarcity meritocracy as they can provide for all their wants and needs, and what they can't simply provides motivation to prove oneself.. Especially when all the other Conventions are put in their place as functional units of the Syndicate-as-Union or are properly disposed of as unecessary. (And, yes, that is a very definite end goal as the Syndicate's current structure and goals are set forth).</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I get that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1071320#post1071320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ascension is just mouthing the relevant dogma. I don't think most Syndicate personnel give it two shakes unless they need to use it for in-Union spin. Ascension is pretty much a cipher in Mage that stands for &quot;what we say we want&quot; but that no one really seems to. Pretty much no organization or individual depicted has any real desire to spend time or effort to achieve it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree here. From what I read, they are very much serious about taking control of reality by taking control of the masses<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1071320#post1071320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is capitalism a tool they intend to discard at some point? They seem awfully invested in it. As in, shoving it down the world's collective throat since before the High Guild showed up for that first meeting of the Order of Reason, on through all that imperialism and down to the present where they have managed to successfully capitalize every alternative method of resource allocation that anyone else has come up with. Oh, and take credit for coming up with it as they bowdlerize it to make it function withing the constraints of the profit motive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, they don't take credit for creating capitalism. They just found that everyone invested so much belief in it that it is currently the best tool for getting what they want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1071320#post1071320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you take control of the world without being ruthless? The answer is implicit in the question. By not being ruthless. By not supporting endeavors that victimize people and move things further and further away from your purported goals (such as, I dunno, CRIME).</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair points in that context. They could use less of the crime bit. There are some complexities with regards to that, but this is really where they start screwing up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1071320#post1071320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By using your powers of persuasion and creation of value in a positive manner. In really promoting a post-scarcity economy in an egalitarian meritocratic society</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all well and good to say this, but how exactly? I mean, what steps should they take? What should they be doing? A suggested plan would be nice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1071320#post1071320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(which means playing nice with NWO instead of trying to undermine them to the point of irrelevance... which won't work really, economy and governments are inextricably intertwined at a fundamental level that exists at all levels of human society)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm at a loss to see how playing nice with the NWO will get them anywhere, considering the NWO loves to push its own agenda on the rest of the technocracy and also brainwash people. Actually how will playing nice with the NWO accomplish anything for them actually?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1071320#post1071320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that would entail some really selfless beneficent thinking and, the proof isn't in the pudding, it's in the eating. They AREN'T selfless, they are the very benchmark of greedy. They AREN'T beneficent, they are the very definition of selfish.</div> </div> </div> </div>If someone said they were selfless, it wasn't me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1071320#post1071320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Sweatshops&quot; aren't called that per se, but they are implicit in the descriptions of the ways that Primal Utility can be used. Particularly in the Syndicate book. Sure you COULD invest in a wonderful little start-up that makes an ap that creates joy or work with the VE to create shipyards for new Voidships that could become partially self-sustaining feedback loops where the Quint harvested could go into the Device creation, but that's not what ends up happening if you want to show the boss that you can add to the Syndicate's Quint stockpiles and invest in their ability to keep the power of the purse going strong and keep a tight rein on the other Conventions.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, the use of Primal Ventures means you gain quintessence by doing business. You visit, buy from, manage, invest in, or otherwise do business with some company or organization. It says nothing about how the business runs or how hard the people in it work. You gain more quintessence not by working these things harder but by visiting , buying from, managing, investing in, or otherwise doing business with more of these.<br /> <br /> Thus your quintessence collection relies on the size of the entities you are dealing with, your Primal Utility Rating, and how much money and work you can put into these. It does not increase with working your people harder. These are normal businesses and organizations they are dealing with. It is also explicit in the book that they find working employees to death wasteful, which it is.<br /> <br /> Next, quintessence isn't profit. It's a resource, and like any resource, the Syndicate uses it to gain what they want. Money is more useful to the Syndicate because money can be used to generate quintessence. I have seen no evidence anywhere that members of the Syndicate are encourage to stockpile quintessence, especially since they can get it relatively easily and trade it for favors that give them actual items and power.<br /> <br /> Edit: Looking at this, the best way to game the Primal Ventures system is to have a few dots dots in primal utility, get a decent Resource rating then invest in a few shares each of a large number of public companies. Each such company will be like a level 2 to 3 node. Even without doing this, every business you visit or buy from will be like a level 1 to 2 node if you have Primal utility, so you can also game the system to some degree by going on a weekly shopping spree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1071320#post1071320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They aren't worse that the other Conventions in action. Well, maybe a little, as the effects of their perfidy are felt more than, say, the Progenitors and It-X, which are probably just as cruel, but it tends to be less broadcast to the population as a whole. And maybe a little more than the NWO, though that is a close one. But the emphasis on competition probably puts them a little more to the black than the NWO and it's push for conformity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd seriously rather work with someone who lets me think how I want to think than someone who forces me to think in a certain way, but maybe that's just me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1071320#post1071320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone is worse than the Void Engineers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot contest this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1071320#post1071320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That plan is about as coherent as that of the underwear gnomes in South Park. And seems vague enough to make one think of selling hamburgers with nearly naked women in swimsuits or cars perched on top of mesas that no car could get to without being lowered by a helicopter. Meaning, welcome to our hype and thank you for buying it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, if you want something like a plan outline, it would be something like:<br /> Control the world economy<br /> Gain fine control over the finances of the masses<br /> Use control over the masses to control the belief of the masses<br /> Use the belief of the masses as a tool to solve problems and make the economy of their dreams<br /> Yay, we control reality. That's Ascension enough for us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-02-2017, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T09:48:40-07:00","id":1071737,"title":"","content":"I'd wager that the Enforcers, at the very least out of the Syndicate, could definitely be called objectively bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T21:22:41-07:00","id":1072354,"title":"","content":"I agree in that they're fearsome criminals, but it can be argued that the Enforcers are the less murdery of all the magely muscle out there. I mean, they mostly use intimidation and fear, they rarely go for the killing plasma shot<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shushu</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the Prime 3 Rotes for Chorus and Verbena has human/animal sacrifice. A rote is an application, not a display of the ideals of the group.</div> </div> </div> </div>A bad example, since both the Verbena and the Celestial Chorus have sacrifice ingrained in their ideals.<br /> <br /> In concrete, for the Celestial Chorus there's the value of self-sacrifice that's very cherished. And the Verbena are all about the power of blood and life, and thus death and sacrifices.<br /> These rotes you mention are deeply ingrained in the belief systems of these Traditions, they represent what their believe about the value of life and death (and how can be manipulated, moraly or not). Their Ideals can't be reconstructed by these rotes, but they're crossed by them.<br /> <br /> Anycase, my point was that the Syndicate it's no stranger to do evil. That's why I pointed that Mages are individuals first and foremost. Saying that &quot;the syndicate it's evil&quot; by denying that they ever do anything for the ideals they supposedly have it's unjust, but saying that &quot;no, hold on, they're noble&quot; hides a very perverse structure of exploitation, that includes and trassends the Rote I mentioned (which it's far from the darkest aspect of the Syndicate), under a *very* small shadow of pink idealism.<br /> <br /> It's no wonder that the Syndicate it's like that, Mages have big egos and are very idealistic, but power corrupts, and resourceful Mages can become quite powerful. The fact it's, in the end, that Masters tend to be self-serving more often than not (even when they will claim the contrary), and they aren't above using the ideals to manipulate the young into doing the stupid and the unmentionable","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-03-2017, 12:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T21:40:19-07:00","id":1072357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, the use of Primal Ventures means you gain quintessence by doing business.<br /> ...<br /> It does not increase with working your people harder.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it may be important to note that Primal Ventures aren't the only way to get Quint by Primal Utility. You can extract the Quint from your overworked employees much like an Extatic can suck the life force with sex. This it's bad/wrong because you weaken them, and I guess not all Syndicate members do it...but hey, it's faster and less costly than sucking Ventures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T05:43:10-07:00","id":1072471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1072357#post1072357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it may be important to note that Primal Ventures aren't the only way to get Quint by Primal Utility. You can extract the Quint from your overworked employees much like an Extatic can suck the life force with sex. This it's bad/wrong because you weaken them, and I guess not all Syndicate members do it...but hey, it's faster and less costly than sucking Ventures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you propose a system or mechanic for this rote? I haven't quite found one. At this point, I can't compare the Primal Ventures to what you are talking about.<br /> <br /> With Primal Ventures, at Primal Utility 2 or 3, purchasing 120 shares of stock in different companies with values of $20 dollars or less will give you the equivalent of 120 Nodes at level 2 to 3 while you are invested in them. Assuming each node gives 4 times its rating a week (Magic is not dying), this gives you 960 to 1440 quintessence a week for an initial investment of less than $2400. That's at least 137 a day, and it just rolls in while you own the shares. With this sort of thing possible, weakening your employees seems like setting your organization up for failure for a minimal return.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-03-2017, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T17:02:33-07:00","id":1072781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1066537#post1066537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as the Syndicate's model goes, people, as in the mass of Sleepers that generate the Consensus, are, with rare exceptions, completely fungible. Such exceptions do not work in Syndicate sweatshops/Quint farms. Not working your employees to death makes no sense, if working them to death will generate a profit.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I desire only money and power. Unpresentable employees give me neither.&quot; Shere Khan, TaleSpin episode Citizen Khan.<br /> <br /> Working your employees to death will cease to generate a profit once you run out of employees; so if you want <i>sustained</i> profits, you'll take care of your employees. In terms of Primal Ventures, this is represented by &quot;don't try to extract too much Primal Utility from a Venture&quot;. Also, Primal Ventures are founded on innovation and industriousness; damage these factors, and you weaken the Venture. Conversely, <i>encourage</i> these factors and you strengthen the Venture, making it more profitable. <br /> <br /> It's not a perfect solution, since the profit motive is a poor substitute for a moral compass. But if you start with and maintain a strong moral compass, you can supplement it with the profit motive as a tool to figure out how best to achieve the aims that your moral compass dictates. <i>That</i> can produce heroic Syndics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T17:53:12-07:00","id":1072818,"title":"","content":"Look at Hank Scorpio from the Simpson's, sure he's an evil mastermind who takes over part of the east cost but he really went to great lengths to care for his employees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T18:16:18-07:00","id":1072837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1072781#post1072781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I desire only money and power. Unpresentable employees give me neither.&quot; Shere Khan, TaleSpin episode Citizen Khan.<br /> <br /> Working your employees to death will cease to generate a profit once you run out of employees; so if you want <i>sustained</i> profits, you'll take care of your employees. In terms of Primal Ventures, this is represented by &quot;don't try to extract too much Primal Utility from a Venture&quot;. Also, Primal Ventures are founded on innovation and industriousness; damage these factors, and you weaken the Venture. Conversely, <i>encourage</i> these factors and you strengthen the Venture, making it more profitable.<br /> <br /> It's not a perfect solution, since the profit motive is a poor substitute for a moral compass. But if you start with and maintain a strong moral compass, you can supplement it with the profit motive as a tool to figure out how best to achieve the aims that your moral compass dictates. <i>That</i> can produce heroic Syndics.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you will never, ever, ever, EVER run out of employees.<br /> <br /> The herd is large.<br /> <br /> If employees ARE fungible and you waste resources on them, you are doing exactly that, WASTING resources and reducing profit, decreasing value. The Venture should be as minimal as possible so that investment creates maximum return. The employees are irrelevant besides their functionality. The product is irrelevant since the actual product is the process as it is the process that allows the Venture to create Quintessence.<br /> <br /> All this emphasis on irrelevant externalities.... Remember the duty to the shareholders to demonstrate maximum results.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T19:47:25-07:00","id":1072887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1072837#post1072837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But you will never, ever, ever, EVER run out of employees.<br /> <br /> The herd is large.<br /> <br /> If employees ARE fungible and you waste resources on them, you are doing exactly that, WASTING resources and reducing profit, decreasing value. The Venture should be as minimal as possible so that investment creates maximum return. The employees are irrelevant besides their functionality. The product is irrelevant since the actual product is the process as it is the process that allows the Venture to create Quintessence.<br /> <br /> All this emphasis on irrelevant externalities.... Remember the duty to the shareholders to demonstrate maximum results.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have thought Syndicate has no shareholders over themselves...? Syndicate is not a simple corporation like Pentex, nor Giovanni dependent on investment of Clan Elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T04:40:32-07:00","id":1073030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1072837#post1072837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But you will never, ever, ever, EVER run out of employees.<br /> <br /> The herd is large.<br /> <br /> If employees ARE fungible and you waste resources on them, you are doing exactly that, WASTING resources and reducing profit, decreasing value. The Venture should be as minimal as possible so that investment creates maximum return. The employees are irrelevant besides their functionality. The product is irrelevant since the actual product is the process as it is the process that allows the Venture to create Quintessence.<br /> <br /> All this emphasis on irrelevant externalities.... Remember the duty to the shareholders to demonstrate maximum results.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which, as always, assumes that working people do death is the most effective and efficient way to get potential out of them. An employee who dies in 5 years will almost certainly not give you as much Quintessence as an employee who dies in 60. Especially if you are investing time and energy in improving their productivity. Employees who die take every bit of that investment with them.<br /> <br /> Sure the output of seven and a half billion people worked to death is pretty impressive, but its nothing compared to the output of seven and a half billion people with the proper training, planning, and investment in the project.<br /> <br /> Sure, that takes time, but the Syndicate isn't just interested in the output of today, it wants to make sure there is even more tomorrow. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T07:22:17-07:00","id":1073104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1072837#post1072837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But you will never, ever, ever, EVER run out of employees.<br /> <br /> The herd is large.<br /> <br /> If employees ARE fungible and you waste resources on them, you are doing exactly that, WASTING resources and reducing profit, decreasing value. The Venture should be as minimal as possible so that investment creates maximum return. The employees are irrelevant besides their functionality. The product is irrelevant since the actual product is the process as it is the process that allows the Venture to create Quintessence.<br /> <br /> All this emphasis on irrelevant externalities.... Remember the duty to the shareholders to demonstrate maximum results.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Syndicate has no shareholders. The highest levels of the Syndicate answered only to Control. Control doesn't care how much quintessence you have. It only cared that you followed its step by step plan for ascension. Control is gone. The Syndicate is no longer controlled by a higher power.<br /> <br /> Primal Ventures can make more quintessence. You don't even need to have employees. If you use the stock market, you need a small initial investment (1 share) for the equivalent of node 2 to 3. You can get as many of these as there are publicly trade-able companies. If you really want to be cheap, you can be your own stock broker. In fact, if you control a big company, you are better off making sure your employees are at the peak of their game because each small business you sell to regularly (establish a contract with) can be the equivalent of node 1, each medium business a node 2, and larger ones node 3. Each small business you buy from can be the equivalent of node 1, each medium business a node 2, and larger ones node 3. Even bigger businesses you deal with provide more quintessence. You want to buy from and sell to the most businesses possible and this won't happen when some of your sales people keeps getting sick, or you suffer delays or quality loss to your product due to employees being less than they can be.<br /> <br /> The herd is large but not infinite. Your recruitment capability is also limited. Your human resources are contested by the other members of the Technocracy as well as the other powers that be in the world of darkness. These other powers will also pounce on parts of your organization that grow too weak. You do not want entire sections of your organization to be pirated because they can get a better, safer deal elsewhere.<br /> <br /> None of what you say seems supported by any of the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-04-2017, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T16:57:54-07:00","id":1073433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1072471#post1072471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you propose a system or mechanic for this rote? I haven't quite found one. At this point, I can't compare the Primal Ventures to what you are talking about.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't need to. It's right there in the book.<br /> <br /> 1rst: You have the Rote I mentioned. <b>An Uncompromising Commitment to Excellence</b> <i>(Syndicate revised p. 82-83)</i> not only makes your workers work hard as fuck, and with an excelent output, but also gives you 5 points of Quintessence per woker that you literally killed with overwork.<br /> <br /> 2nd: Primal Utility 3 <i>&quot;Living Asset Exploitation&quot; </i>allows to :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Syndicate revised p.80</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">harvest Primal Energy from deceased living things, such as specially raised livestock or employees he literally works to death. The Technocrat cannot \u201cdrain life\u201d directly, but seizes its power at the moment of death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, Verbena/Nephandi like human sacrifice, but in a Technocratically approved way. You can't extract Quintessence of your employes without killing them at this level (I tought this was possible), but you can do it at higher levels (and there's systems for it, 1 Quint per Aggravated level inflicted, as per PU 5, just use a variation of the rote &quot;An Uncompromising Commitment to Excellence&quot; that has PU 5 instead of 3. That way you do not need to kill them to get the juice, albeit you can).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-04-2017, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T17:09:10-07:00","id":1073442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1073104#post1073104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Syndicate has no shareholders. The highest levels of the Syndicate answered only to Control. Control doesn't care how much quintessence you have. It only cared that you followed its step by step plan for ascension. Control is gone. The Syndicate is no longer controlled by a higher power.<br /> <br /> Primal Ventures can make more quintessence. You don't even need to have employees. If you use the stock market, you need a small initial investment (1 share) for the equivalent of node 2 to 3. You can get as many of these as there are publicly trade-able companies. If you really want to be cheap, you can be your own stock broker. In fact, if you control a big company, you are better off making sure your employees are at the peak of their game because each small business you sell to regularly (establish a contract with) can be the equivalent of node 1, each medium business a node 2, and larger ones node 3. Each small business you buy from can be the equivalent of node 1, each medium business a node 2, and larger ones node 3. Even bigger businesses you deal with provide more quintessence. You want to buy from and sell to the most businesses possible and this won't happen when some of your sales people keeps getting sick, or you suffer delays or quality loss to your product due to employees being less than they can be.<br /> <br /> The herd is large but not infinite. Your recruitment capability is also limited. Your human resources are contested by the other members of the Technocracy as well as the other powers that be in the world of darkness. These other powers will also pounce on parts of your organization that grow too weak. You do not want entire sections of your organization to be pirated because they can get a better, safer deal elsewhere.<br /> <br /> None of what you say seems supported by any of the books.</div> </div> </div> </div> 7+ billion people is more than enough for my infinitely deadly sweatshop and still, oh, I dunno, BILLIONS left over for everyone else to play with. Plus, they keep making more of themselves. Hence &quot;fungible&quot;. Hence, the &quot;herd is large&quot;. For these purposes, the herd isn't just large, it's nigh infinite. <br /> <br /> If I am running a sweatshop, I HAVE superiors I AM answerable to them. My sweatshop does not equal either the entire Syndicate or the world. If am not surpassing my production quota, I can assue you that there are other Syndicate sweatshop operators that ARE meeting theirs and they are angling for MORE (because who doesn't want MORE). Tearing me down is de jure, particularly, if I don't have what it takes to do what it takes to get the job done. So I have every incentive to do absolutely awful things and pretty much NONE of the things that you are saying will hold me back are worth it. Those are losing strategies. And this is a game. Winners get everything and losers get absolutely fucking nothing (except for, possibly, a seat at a station in their successors sweatshop). I don't have time for a conscience and, honestly, it's probably going to get me killed to have one. Or worse. <br /> <br /> Quintessence is the ONLY thing that matters if this is about the sweatshop Primal Venture. That's why we're even DOING this. Having the biggest piles of Quint leads to being the primary distribution network of Quint, the need for the creation of Devices (et al.) being a very very important matter in the Union (nigh mission critical) means everyone else wants what the Syndicate has. Want Void Ships, VE's? We can get you the Quint from those sweatshop Ventures. Want every MiB to have MirrorShades NWO? We can get you the Quint for that. Need juice for the power cell in your cybernetics, It-X? The Syndicate has you covered. Etc. <br /> <br /> Aside from all that: The problem with the Syndicate vis-a-vis &quot;evil&quot; is that, any and all propoganda aside, the Syndicate IS capitalism and never has been anything else, even when it was the High Guild. There really aren't any other arrows in their quivers. Any other means of resource allocation is pretty much something they are trying to co-opt and capitalize (meaning, &quot;bring it under our umbrella&quot;) or they are systems that don't scale to the level they want to work at (mutualism, barter, etc.). And the problems with capitalism is that it does reward selfish behavior. In fact, it does more than that, it actually negatively incentivizes altruistic behavior Which can lead to a fairly unpleasant negative homeostatic feedback loop unless it is really, really constrained. Ideally, Control might do that. The whole system of the Union does do that to a degree by setting the Syndicate into a symbiosis with the other Conventions. And the direction as set by the leaders of the Syndicate proper might check it as well. But, inherently, those checks will break down and you'll end up getting the Syndicate doing BAD BAD things. Like SPD. Like being the festering nest-hole of the Technephandi. Like the Syndicate becoming the ur-Union by trying to co-opt the roles that the other Conventions are supposed to play by having in-house R&amp;D (to offset interdependence with It-X &amp; Progenitors) or by undermining the biggest check on their bad behavior by undermining various sorts of governmental power (from fascism to democracy) with plutocracy.<br /> <br /> Which is kind of funny, because mages are pretty much 100% a potential post-scarcity functional group with relatively low levels of Matter (and Life... but Matter will do just fine) EXCEPT for Quint. And the Syndicate, with Primal Ventures, actually have a way to create enough of that to offset that. (E.g. include the Primal Venture as an integral part of the use of the Quintessence and you have something of an ouroborous.) <br /> <br /> But, really, aside from what they SAY about their alleged goals, they haven't really shown any inclination to make that happen. Not even for themselves. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T19:55:09-07:00","id":1073516,"title":"","content":"I hate Syndicate. I even more hate all-powerful, nigh-omnipotent uber Syndicate portrayed in revised and M20.<br /> <br /> Even then, I think SPD and Technephandi thing was deliberately created by WW to demonize the Syndicate, the Union, the Capitalism, and by extension, modern industrial and capitalistic civilization itself. They fill 'bad bad amoral capitalistic plutocracy' role along with Pentex.<br /> <br /> Technephandi I could somewhat understand, however SPD is so utterly contrived, incongruous, incompatible crossover that it makes laugh of the Syndicate, the Union, and even Control itself. It makes Union as whole incompetent imbeciles and moronic plaything of Nephandi/Pentex. It also severely undermines core, basic theme, tenet, mood and psyche of MtA in extreme. It shits on universal cosmology of MtA and indirectly vindicate WtA cosmology and belief system are ultimately 'right'. You are wrong, puny humans! Werecreatures are right. Always. Since we are wise and blessed by spirits and humans are petty wrong inferior universe proves it blah blah blah.<br /> <br /> Fundamentally, <b>it literally ruins everything espoused in Mage</b> in and itself.<br /> <br /> In my play and canon, I completely delete SPD. Such vile unnatural ignoble idiotic thing simply does not exist in MtA from the outset. SPD should be in the WtA world, instead of contaminating MtA setting with its stupid deviant toxin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 04-04-2017, 11:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T20:13:11-07:00","id":1073527,"title":"","content":"Personally, I don't delete SPD; I reimagine it by cutting all ties with Werewolf's setting and presenting it as <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009152-spd-a-new-take\">one of the last refuges within the Technocracy for fringe science</a>. No Pentex, no fomorians, no Wyrm Taint; just scientists who try to reconcile the Technocracy's ideals with Etherite-like paradigms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-04-2017, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T21:08:59-07:00","id":1073550,"title":"","content":"On Ajax's recent arguments, they certainly fit the Syndicate as presented in 2e and M20, with the Strong implication that they've been corrupted and represent the worst take on capitalism. I personally prefer a more human Syndicate, with members who cut the profit motive with a healthy dose of ethics and seek long-term profits that help everyone involved over exploitative practices that are good for a quick buck but ultimately destroy the market. Not to say that there aren't bad eggs in the mix; just that you don't have to be a ruthless bastard to succeed in the Syndicate.<br /> <br /> Call it rose-colored glasses if you like. I still prefer it to the worst-case scenario that Ajax has been pushing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExa