 theirs and they are angling for MORE (because who doesn't want MORE). Tearing me down is de jure, particularly, if I don't have what it takes to do what it takes to get the job done. So I have every incentive to do absolutely awful things and pretty much NONE of the things that you are saying will hold me back are worth it. Those are losing strategies. And this is a game. Winners get everything and losers get absolutely fucking nothing (except for, possibly, a seat at a station in their successors sweatshop). I don't have time for a conscience and, honestly, it's probably going to get me killed to have one. Or worse.<br /> <br /> Quintessence is the ONLY thing that matters if this is about the sweatshop Primal Venture. That's why we're even DOING this. Having the biggest piles of Quint leads to being the primary distribution network of Quint, the need for the creation of Devices (et al.) being a very very important matter in the Union (nigh mission critical) means everyone else wants what the Syndicate has. Want Void Ships, VE's? We can get you the Quint from those sweatshop Ventures. Want every MiB to have MirrorShades NWO? We can get you the Quint for that. Need juice for the power cell in your cybernetics, It-X? The Syndicate has you covered. Etc.<br /> <br /> Aside from all that: The problem with the Syndicate vis-a-vis &quot;evil&quot; is that, any and all propoganda aside, the Syndicate IS capitalism and never has been anything else, even when it was the High Guild. There really aren't any other arrows in their quivers. Any other means of resource allocation is pretty much something they are trying to co-opt and capitalize (meaning, &quot;bring it under our umbrella&quot;) or they are systems that don't scale to the level they want to work at (mutualism, barter, etc.). And the problems with capitalism is that it does reward selfish behavior. In fact, it does more than that, it actually negatively incentivizes altruistic behavior Which can lead to a fairly unpleasant negative homeostatic feedback loop unless it is really, really constrained. Ideally, Control might do that. The whole system of the Union does do that to a degree by setting the Syndicate into a symbiosis with the other Conventions. And the direction as set by the leaders of the Syndicate proper might check it as well. But, inherently, those checks will break down and you'll end up getting the Syndicate doing BAD BAD things. Like SPD. Like being the festering nest-hole of the Technephandi. Like the Syndicate becoming the ur-Union by trying to co-opt the roles that the other Conventions are supposed to play by having in-house R&amp;D (to offset interdependence with It-X &amp; Progenitors) or by undermining the biggest check on their bad behavior by undermining various sorts of governmental power (from fascism to democracy) with plutocracy.<br /> <br /> Which is kind of funny, because mages are pretty much 100% a potential post-scarcity functional group with relatively low levels of Matter (and Life... but Matter will do just fine) EXCEPT for Quint. And the Syndicate, with Primal Ventures, actually have a way to create enough of that to offset that. (E.g. include the Primal Venture as an integral part of the use of the Quintessence and you have something of an ouroborous.)<br /> <br /> But, really, aside from what they SAY about their alleged goals, they haven't really shown any inclination to make that happen. Not even for themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel you haven't read any of my arguments. Most everything I've mentioned is in or supported by the books on the topic or a logical extension of such. I could even cite page numbers and tell you how I arrive at these statements if you like.<br /> <br /> The way I read this, you seem to simply assume they use people in a way the Syndicate book says they don't and in a manner Primal Ventures suggests is not optimal on a scale that seems impossible for the Syndicate or any mage group for an objective that makes no sense and is not supported by anything written about them. You equate them to capitalism when it's explicitly stated that they did not invent capitalism but consider it a tool to be used and discarded.<br /> <br /> The entire technocracy has access to Primal Utility, and I posit that primal ventures can be used in a manner that creates more quintessence for them than a group of mages of their size will need in a more efficient way than any other method in Mage.<br /> <br /> We don't even have a system for your supposed sweat shop rote. Again, I don't think of the Syndicate as good guys but this whole sweatshop thing has no basis that I can see in the written material. At this point, I feel I'm only arguing here so that people don't get the wrong impression about the written material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-05-2017, 12:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T21:57:05-07:00","id":1073570,"title":"","content":"To be fair, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> just posted references to where the Revised Syndicate Book references the exploitation Rote and the Effect on which it is based. They do exist. That doesn't mean everyone uses them; as you say, it takes effort to replace lost workers, so even from a strictly utilitarian point of view it's not clear that subjecting your employees to its full force is <i>the</i> thing to do. <br /> <br /> And like I said in my last post, I don't buy the notion that the Syndicate <i>must</i> be presented as a worst-case caricature of capitalism. Heck, what @Ajax is describing sounds more like what I'd expect of the Threat Null counterpart to the Syndicate, where their humanity has been stripped away and all that's left is an urge to make money at all costs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T22:46:36-07:00","id":1073585,"title":"","content":"SPD is simply disgusting. It is a hideous blemish of setting. It is an abomination. It is better to be forgotten, to be obliterated from everyone's memory.<br /> <br /> And while M20 Syndicate is definitely worse than revised one, It is rather doubtful M20 Syndics are indeed a worst-case caricature of corrupted capitalism portrayed in 2e. They are not <i>that </i>bad, not nearly. Hell, in 1st and 2rd, Technocracy was as bad as Vampires, Pentex and Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T23:01:06-07:00","id":1073591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1073433#post1073433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I don't need to. It's right there in the book..</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1073570#post1073570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> just posted references to where the Revised Syndicate Book references the exploitation Rote and the Effect on which it is based. They do exist. That doesn't mean everyone uses them; as you say, it takes effort to replace lost workers, so even from a strictly utilitarian point of view it's not clear that subjecting your employees to its full force is <i>the</i> thing to do.<br /> <br /> And like I said in my last post, I don't buy the notion that the Syndicate <i>must</i> be presented as a worst-case caricature of capitalism. Heck, what @Ajax is describing sounds more like what I'd expect of the Threat Null counterpart to the Syndicate, where their humanity has been stripped away and all that's left is an urge to make money at all costs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi, My apologies. I missed these completely and it seems I've been looking at the older book... apparently, I don't have the revised version of the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-05-2017, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T00:07:13-07:00","id":1073600,"title":"","content":"Now, a direct comparison.<br /> <br /> Let's say you, a member of the Syndicate, have a mid-sized business with 250 employees with an annual revenue of $66,000,000. Let's say it has a profit of 5% $3,300,000 annually. ($68750 a week)<br /> <br /> You can kill 225 employees to gain 1125 quintessence. This will probably screw up your company, kill profits, and get you on the news and sued. Or at least other groups will take advantage...<br /> <br /> or you can take your $68750 profit in one week and invest using Primal ventures in $20 or less of a share each in a medium businesses to get 6875 quintessence a week in a world where magick is dying. In a world where magick is not dying, this becomes 27500 quintessence. You can do the same thing next week and increase your weekly quintessence gain by the same amount.<br /> <br /> If your business is stable, you can also use primal ventures so that every business you sell to or buy from (regularly) also gets you 1 quintessence a week in a world where magick is dying or 4 in a world where it isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-05-2017, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T06:38:42-07:00","id":1073696,"title":"","content":"An Uncompromising Commitment to Excellence: not every Syndic is going to be able to use this. It requires ten dots worth of Spheres: four in Mind, three in Life, and three in Primal Utility. As a source of Primal Energy, it's inefficient; if your goal is to extract Quintessence from humans by killing them, you're better off reskinning an actual human sacrifice effect in technocratic terms: you'll get twice as much Q per victim. As well, the Uncompromising Commitment rote is unreliable, as each victim gets multiple chances to resist. And again, that's not counting any of the social consequences of employing this rote. Frankly, it's more suitable for use as an emergency measure than as a routine Procedure. <br /> <br /> A more reliable source of Q is the Node, Juncture, or Primal Venture. As long as you treat them well (i.e., don't try to take too much Primal Energy too quickly), Nodes and Ventures provide an ongoing source of Primal Energy. You also don't need nearly as much Sphere knowledge. The &quot;downside&quot; is that they're not commonplace: Ventures, in particular, need to embody human innovation in a truly exceptional fashion. While rare, this means that investing in Primal Ventures almost by definition involves improving society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T07:15:05-07:00","id":1073706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1073696#post1073696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;downside&quot; is that they're not commonplace: Ventures, in particular, need to embody human innovation in a truly exceptional fashion. While rare, this means that investing in Primal Ventures almost by definition involves improving society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, would you mind clarifying this? From my reading of M20, you turn a business into a node and there's no mention of rarity. Is this mentioned in Syndicate revised? Also, the primal ventures chart seems to include organized crime alongside normal businesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T07:32:22-07:00","id":1073713,"title":"","content":"It's from the Revised Convention Book, where Primal Utility first appeared.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T07:38:43-07:00","id":1073715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, a direct comparison.<br /> <br /> Let's say you, a member of the Syndicate, have a mid-sized business with 250 employees with an annual revenue of $66,000,000. Let's say it has a profit of 5% $3,300,000 annually. ($68750 a week)<br /> <br /> You can kill 225 employees to gain 1125 quintessence. This will probably screw up your company, kill profits, and get you on the news and sued. Or at least other groups will take advantage...<br /> <br /> or you can take your $68750 profit in one week and invest using Primal ventures in $20 or less of a share each in a medium businesses to get 6875 quintessence a week in a world where magick is dying. In a world where magick is not dying, this becomes 27500 quintessence. You can do the same thing next week and increase your weekly quintessence gain by the same amount.<br /> <br /> If your business is stable, you can also use primal ventures so that every business you sell to or buy from (regularly) also gets you 1 quintessence a week in a world where magick is dying or 4 in a world where it isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's my understanding that you can do<b> <i>neither</i></b>. Because you're ignoring the difficulty of A. Casting a spell with that many successes (well, you could do it if you work yourself to death casting all days of the week, but then you're going to botch a lot of times), and B. attaining 6875 Ventures in a world where:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ventures, in particular, need to embody human innovation in a truly exceptional fashion. While rare, this means that investing in Primal Ventures almost by definition involves improving society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not every bar it's a Venture, most bars probably aren't a Venture. You will need to travel arround the world (or use Data/Corr, which implies A to some extent) to get that many Ventures. And remember that Syndicate members other that you exist and may want to collect Quintessence too. <br /> <br /> <br /> Besides, you and Dataweaver aren't geting into the spirit of having a Sweatshop.<br /> <br /> A sweatshop it's a place where lots of people people works mechanically, doing things that <i>don't require any capacitation</i>. The only limit to the amount of people that you can employ there it's the limit of space you have, literaly millons of unemployed are waiting to enter. Usually they're illegal to begin with, so there's no control. Even then, killing 200+ people a week probably it's going to get some atention, but a few deaths per month/week can pass. It probably isn't a Venture, albeit it could if it was, say, the first industry of that population. You don't need to be there all the time to use a (potentially easier?) variant of the Rote using PU 3, just use the slavers managers as Focus, so you can go to other sweatshops and/or to exploit a few Ventures.<br /> <br /> The real problem it's the fact that you're basically a Technephandi, with all the Jhor you will surelly acumulate. But well, you probably weren't a good person to begin with.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T07:38:48-07:00","id":1073716,"title":"","content":"Ah. In M20, it seems to say you turn a mundane business into a node. It gave no further conditions. It seems I'm looking at a different set of rules. I'm inclined to think M20 is replacing the old rules... the alternative being someone made a huge mistake in rewriting Primal Ventures.<br /> <br /> Just to mention: if you worked at it in 2 sets of 3 hour-long rituals a day, 5 days a week, with an average of 2 successes per roll, you are likely to get 60 successes a week. So, for a typical starting character, having access to any more than 60 quintessence a week from any type or number of sources will usually be pointless.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-05-2017, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T07:44:25-07:00","id":1073719,"title":"","content":"PU 1 Allows to &quot;sense a Venture&quot; . That would be silly if you can just enter a bar and use it as a Venture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T08:00:46-07:00","id":1073724,"title":"","content":"In M20 there is Assess PU, Deposit PU, and Exploit PU as part of PU1. I'm assuming this is to assess the level of a venture (and its equivalent node rating), deposit quintessence, and use quintessence. It says nothing about detection or finding a Venture. At least I don't see it in there.<br /> <br /> Edit: Aslo, rules aside, I don't see that as silly. It's a business through which money flows. Virtually every person in the world has a bit of invested belief in money. From this comes power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-05-2017, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T09:03:17-07:00","id":1073749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1073600#post1073600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, a direct comparison.<br /> <br /> Let's say you, a member of the Syndicate, have a mid- business with 250 employees with an annual revenue of $66,000,000. Let's say it has a profit of 5% $3,300,000 annually. ($68750 a week)<br /> <br /> You can kill 225 employees to gain 1125 quintessence. This will probably screw up your company, kill profits, and get you on the news and sued. Or at least other groups will take advantage...<br /> <br /> or you can take your $68750 profit in one week and invest using Primal ventures in $20 or less of a share each in a medium businesses to get 6875 quintessence a week in a world where magick is dying. In a world where magick is not dying, this becomes 27500 quintessence. You can do the same thing next week and increase your weekly quintessence gain by the same amount.<br /> <br /> If your business is stable, you can also use primal ventures so that every business you sell to or buy from (regularly) also gets you 1 quintessence a week in a world where magick is dying or 4 in a world where it isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Errr.... Those numbers seem way off. WAY off. As in, Ventures are supposed to represent an alternative to using a Node. Basically creating a Juncture that needs some elbow grease. Not a Von Neuman Device Quint engine. It's supposed to leads to the Syndicate having a massive advantage in Quintessence allocation because they can actually create Quintessence fairly easily instead of having to mine it (or have a Master around who can create a mine). So, depending on where you slice it, maybe, high end, dozens of Quint per week. (And, though that does sound like a lot, take a look at what it required to make a Voidship or mass produce the standard array of gadgets a baseline actual mage MiB is carrying around....) <br /> <br /> I mean, I guess you CAN also run the business as less of a sweatshop and more of an assembly line Aztec-style human sacrifice Venture and mine the Quint out of the patterns of your workers as you drop them. However, your Resonance is going to go from &quot;Dreary&quot; to &quot;Hello Mr. Wyrm! We have a corner office waiting for you!&quot; And that causes huge problems with whatever Devices or Procedures that Quint ends up getting used for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T09:19:12-07:00","id":1073754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1073550#post1073550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Ajax's recent arguments, they certainly fit the Syndicate as presented in 2e and M20, with the Strong implication that they've been corrupted and represent the worst take on capitalism. I personally prefer a more human Syndicate, with members who cut the profit motive with a healthy dose of ethics and seek long-term profits that help everyone involved over exploitative practices that are good for a quick buck but ultimately destroy the market. Not to say that there aren't bad eggs in the mix; just that you don't have to be a ruthless bastard to succeed in the Syndicate.<br /> <br /> Call it rose-colored glasses if you like. I still prefer it to the worst-case scenario that Ajax has been pushing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thread is &quot;Is the Syndicate Evil?&quot;, right?<br /> <br /> So, near logical extreme end is a good way to test that answer. A devil's adovacate position as it were. <br /> <br /> Unfortunately, unless your personal WoD is very very different from the actual world and the way things tend to fall out, the Syndicate is going to be very precariously balanced with regard to sliding down the slippery slope to something like &quot;evil&quot;. That's just how this sort of thing works. You have to have powerful incentives and disincentives in place in this kind of system for it not to fall out of whack and become a race to the bottom. <br /> <br /> I think the Syndicate as written can represent that. They have more problems with other Conventions with their ethical barometer and where that needle ends up depends on which Syndicate you want to have. Most of the time, outside of the Syndicate books, the Syndicate definitely trends to the &quot;shady if not actually outright bad guys&quot;. I don't pay a lot of attention to what they say about themselves because they are the best salesmen around. So, of course, they think they're the GREATEST THING EVER. And totally helping out everyone! Yup, yup! But, I definitely think there is room for a better and more balanced Syndicate than I (and a vast majority of the books, definitely including the Syndicate~= Technephandi of M20) where some of the hype is actually true, there are incentives and disincentives in place to keep a significant portion of the membership on a semi-ethical path. But even then, there is going to be a dark underbelly where profit (not really money, more 'Creation of Value) is pursued with no ethics at all The question is how deeply do you have to bury your skeletons to stay in the game if your are going to indulge in some flensing now and again. <br /> <br /> FYI, the Syndicate as portrayed in my games has varied from one side to the other. In the current game, they are VERY opportunistic, but they are also not complete douches about it. The entire group of mixed Tradition and Union mages have just been suborned in an internal coup in a Syndicate Amalgam, which could end up in having this Syndicate group fissioning off and seeking asylum from the OoH as a new House (more &quot;financial wizards&quot; and less &quot;gambling wizards&quot; like the Fortunae). In any case, they are being really good to the PCs and enabling them in a lot of ways to achieve their objectives. In turn, later, a chunk of the PCs will be helping the faction in the Amalgam helping them to achieve their objectives.<br /> <br /> In previous games, the Syndicate were the active bogeyman of one character's history and, when and where they showed up, were total asshats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T09:26:59-07:00","id":1073761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1073715#post1073715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A sweatshop it's a place where lots of people people works mechanically, doing things that <i>don't require any capacitation</i>. The only limit to the amount of people that you can employ there it's the limit of space you have, literaly millons of unemployed are waiting to enter. Usually they're illegal to begin with, so there's no control. Even then, killing 200+ people a week probably it's going to get some atention, but a few deaths per month/week can pass. It probably isn't a Venture, albeit it could if it was, say, the first industry of that population. You don't need to be there all the time to use a (potentially easier?) variant of the Rote using PU 3, just use the slavers managers as Focus, so you can go to other sweatshops and/or to exploit a few Ventures.<br /> <br /> The real problem it's the fact that you're basically a Technephandi, with all the Jhor you will surelly acumulate. But well, you probably weren't a good person to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sure could be a Venture. Just because it's creative, effectively creating &quot;Value&quot;, doesn't mean it has to be ethical. I'm not buying into Dataweaver saying a Venture has to make society better. Why? In fact, HOW? There are always externalities, costs to both the people involved and those outside of the Venture. And sometimes those costs aren't ones that were willingly and knowingly accepted. Meaning they were imposed without the will of those in the payer position. Also called, &quot;victimization&quot; if it gets to a certain (any?) point.<br /> <br /> If Ventures require being completely wholesome, there aren't many of them at all. <br /> <br /> And, you don't have to kill them, you can just fire them when they can't hack it anymore. And the production can be widgets of absolutely no value, you're just doing it in a novel way that is producing something, even if it's intangibles (Look at all the people working! Look at that old building being used! Look at all the pretty, shiny, useless, easily breakable trinkets!) <br /> <br /> In which case, no Jhor. Maybe some kind of Static Resonance, but even it's something like &quot;boring&quot;, it might just be hella useful for specific purposes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T09:59:49-07:00","id":1073781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sure could be a Venture. Just because it's creative, effectively creating &quot;Value&quot;, doesn't mean it has to be ethical. I'm not buying into Dataweaver saying a Venture has to make society better. Why? In fact, HOW?</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither am I. &quot;Better&quot; it's used in the book as something relative to the Sydicate's Paradigm, it could be &quot;worse&quot; for another Paradigm. Example: A successful private school that gives prestige to people that study there, but it's too expensive for most people to enter, and isn't really better at &quot;education&quot; than public institutes (in the sense that it's level isn't very high), could still be a successful Venture<br /> <br /> <i>However, we must take &quot;Value&quot; as something the Syndicate would &quot;think&quot; would make the society better</i>. Sweatshops have (sadly, unsurprisingly) it's defenders, as they generate labor for people that otherwise would be left aside, are cheap, and can represent beneffits for multinational corporations. One can argue that China built their economic power partially thanks to this &quot;models&quot;, so yes, it can be a Venture. But it doesn't need to. If there's nothing new, nothing that represents a big potential in the business. Nothing &quot;<i>venturous</i>&quot;, so to speak. It wouldn't be the focus for economical value and prosperity that the Venture it's supposed to represent.<br /> I don't see things becoming a Venture just because it produces any amount of proffit . Otherwise every grocery and fast-food store it's a Venture, and then you can run with Saikou's projections (which I think makes Quint a tad too common for my liking, even for the $yndicate)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-05-2017, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T10:22:56-07:00","id":1073785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1073749#post1073749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Errr.... Those numbers seem way off. WAY off. As in, Ventures are supposed to represent an alternative to using a Node. Basically creating a Juncture that needs some elbow grease. Not a Von Neuman Device Quint engine. It's supposed to leads to the Syndicate having a massive advantage in Quintessence allocation because they can actually create Quintessence fairly easily instead of having to mine it (or have a Master around who can create a mine). So, depending on where you slice it, maybe, high end, dozens of Quint per week. (And, though that does sound like a lot, take a look at what it required to make a Voidship or mass produce the standard array of gadgets a baseline actual mage MiB is carrying around....)<br /> <br /> I mean, I guess you CAN also run the business as less of a sweatshop and more of an assembly line Aztec-style human sacrifice Venture and mine the Quint out of the patterns of your workers as you drop them. However, your Resonance is going to go from &quot;Dreary&quot; to &quot;Hello Mr. Wyrm! We have a corner office waiting for you!&quot; And that causes huge problems with whatever Devices or Procedures that Quint ends up getting used for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently I've been reading a different rule set from everyone else. If you do a reading of M20 and nothing else though, it seems to suggest what I said. Whether that is author intent or an enormous screw up is another matter altogether. But it's there and completely use-able as a set of rules for turning &quot;mundane businesses&quot; into nodes with no mention of any other qualities of the business. Either way. Very few mages can make use of or even process more than 60 quintessence a week, working almost full time at it, so I think we're taking this problem beyond it's logical optimal point in both our cases. Assuming there are around 2000 mages in the Syndicate, they would likely choke on any more than 120000 quintessence a week (24000 deaths or a week or 15000 permanent level 2 Primal Ventures)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-05-2017, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T10:58:30-07:00","id":1073799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1073754#post1073754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thread is &quot;Is the Syndicate Evil?&quot;, right?<br /> <br /> So, near logical extreme end is a good way to test that answer. A devil's adovacate position as it were.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't the opposite logical extreme be a better test? A devil's advocate actually looks for every reason not to support the original presupposition. If someone is a candidate for canonization as a saint for example, the Devil's advocate looks for every reason for the person not to be canonized as a saint. If none of the Devil's advocate's arguments have merit, then it could be safely said that the candidate for sainthood can be considered a saint. Otherwise the candidate's sainthood is uncertain.<br /> <br /> A Devil's advocate for &quot;Is the Syndicate Evil&quot; would look for every reason why the Syndicate should not be considered Evil. By this system, if no merit is to be found in the arguments of the Devil's advocate, then the Syndicate can be safely called Evil. If there is merit in even one argument made by the Devil's Advocate, then the Syndicate's Evilness is not certain.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T11:08:00-07:00","id":1073801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1073715#post1073715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, you and Dataweaver aren't geting into the spirit of having a Sweatshop.</div> </div> </div> </div> Why is that a problem?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1073754#post1073754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thread is \u201cIs the Syndicate Evil?\u201d, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cIs the Syndicate Evil?\u201d, not \u201cThe Syndicate is Evil\u201d.<br /> <br /> And a perfectly valid answer to that question is \u201cno\u201d or \u201cno more than anyone else&quot;. Sure you <i>could</i> assume the answer is \u201cyes\u201d; but if that assumption is the only one that you explore, you're going to get a rather one-sided \u201cmustache-twirling villain\u201d view of the Convention. For a more rounded view, you need to consider other options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-05-2017, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T11:27:53-07:00","id":1073806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1073754#post1073754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thread is &quot;Is the Syndicate Evil?&quot;, right?<br /> <br /> So, near logical extreme end is a good way to test that answer. A devil's adovacate position as it were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since it's a question of how they are depicted... not really? There aren't many factions in Mage that can't be depicted as evil if you set your mind to it. Also, how evil they are depends a great deal on unstated assumptions, like what goals you ascribe to the organization, or personal opinions on capitalism and business.<br /> <br /> For instance:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unfortunately, unless your personal WoD is very very different from the actual world and the way things tend to fall out, the Syndicate is going to be very precariously balanced with regard to sliding down the slippery slope to something like &quot;evil&quot;. That's just how this sort of thing works. You have to have powerful incentives and disincentives in place in this kind of system for it not to fall out of whack and become a race to the bottom. </div> </div> </div>I don't see real world businesses constantly teetering on the edge of evil. Which is not to say some don't fall over the edge, but plenty more don't even come close. It is a wide range of behaviors and cultures rather than a single bunch clumped on the edge of the abyss. I'd be much more inclined to ascribe that kind of balancing act to the media or to politicians, but even there I'd have to admit a lot of that is based on the actions of a few.<br /> <br /> It is also worth noting that any time you depict an organization as only caring about one goal (say, profit) you run the risk of turning them into a monomaniacal force that runs over everything in its way. If instead you have them hold several values (say, profit, creating environments for humanity to thrive, searching for potential, etc) they will have more nuance and more scruples in their goals. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T13:06:22-07:00","id":1073848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1073806#post1073806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since it's a question of how they are depicted... not really? There aren't many factions in Mage that can't be depicted as evil if you set your mind to it. Also, how evil they are depends a great deal on unstated assumptions, like what goals you ascribe to the organization, or personal opinions on capitalism and business.<br /> <br /> For instance:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't see real world businesses constantly teetering on the edge of evil. Which is not to say some don't fall over the edge, but plenty more don't even come close. It is a wide range of behaviors and cultures rather than a single bunch clumped on the edge of the abyss. I'd be much more inclined to ascribe that kind of balancing act to the media or to politicians, but even there I'd have to admit a lot of that is based on the actions of a few.<br /> <br /> It is also worth noting that any time you depict an organization as only caring about one goal (say, profit) you run the risk of turning them into a monomaniacal force that runs over everything in its way. If instead you have them hold several values (say, profit, creating environments for humanity to thrive, searching for potential, etc) they will have more nuance and more scruples in their goals.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Was the question &quot;Does the Way the Syndicate is portrayed show them as being evil&quot; you're answer might apply. Not really though as we have TONS of material not in the last Syndicate book that overwhelmingly portrays the Syndicate as not being very nice people at all. <br /> <br /> I don't think they are out there to create profit. They are out there to create &quot;value&quot;. Which they have done repeatedly throughout history by creating several fictions that are incredibly important to daily life for most of humanity, like, &quot;money&quot;. Profit is just a very easy way to measure created value. One that can be easily taught to the newbies who are pre-conditioned to working within the preferred Foci of the Syndicate. <br /> <br /> But scruples, ethics, morals, etc. are NOT an essential part of the mix to create value and, in fact, can get in the way of doing so, particularly if you want to get things done faster. <br /> <br /> One of the reasons that the Syndicate is more prone to corruption is that it embraces competition in many of its ways of accomplishing goals. That can entice people to take the easy way out. If they actually embraced cooperation, like, say, the NWO fundamentally does, then they wouldn't have these particular issues. They would have other, equally disturbing issues. (Like soul-crushing conformity, etc.)<br /> <br /> And, yes, real world business in the sense of capitalism in the sense of competition over limited resources to produce gain ('supply' and 'demand') does inherently have issues in that the bottom will always fall out of it when any participant stops behaving ethically. Starting with the Tragedy of the Commons and moving onwards. To most of the people here it seems to be seen as an inherent bug in the system that they want to wish away. To a lot of very rich people and many economists, it's a design feature, not a flaw. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T13:12:12-07:00","id":1073850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1073801#post1073801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Why is that a problem?<br /> <br /> \u201cIs the Syndicate Evil?\u201d, not \u201cThe Syndicate is Evil\u201d.<br /> <br /> And a perfectly valid answer to that question is \u201cno\u201d or \u201cno more than anyone else&quot;. Sure you <i>could</i> assume the answer is \u201cyes\u201d; but if that assumption is the only one that you explore, you're going to get a rather one-sided \u201cmustache-twirling villain\u201d view of the Convention. For a more rounded view, you need to consider other options.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's how debate works.... And when you come up with counter arguments, I counter them and so on.... <br /> <br /> I took &quot;YES&quot;. I could have taken &quot;NO&quot;, but, really that position has already been amply taken. It's the entirety of the Rev. Syndicate book. <br /> <br /> And, TBH, a completely shiny, gleaming Syndicate that never harmed a fly, is completely misunderstood and it 9/10ths of the way to pampering Humanity to Ascension is actually less interesting to me than a Syndicate that is the birthing hive for the Technephandi. And that's not really very interesting either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T13:25:39-07:00","id":1073856,"title":"","content":"Fallacy of the Excluded Middle. The options aren't \u201ceither they're overrun by Technophandi or they're shining beacons of hope\u201d. There are options in between those extremes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T07:15:07-07:00","id":1074114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1073848#post1073848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Was the question &quot;Does the Way the Syndicate is portrayed show them as being evil&quot; you're answer might apply. Not really though as we have TONS of material not in the last Syndicate book that overwhelmingly portrays the Syndicate as not being very nice people at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't change that how the Syndicate is portrayed completely changes their moral status. So choosing a single negative lens to look at them through isn't as useful as, say, looking at the positive depictions of the Syndicate and seeing how they could be twisted. The latter also avoids the two least interesting options, the squeaky clean Syndicate and the wreched hive of scum and villainy Syndicate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think they are out there to create profit. They are out there to create &quot;value&quot;. Which they have done repeatedly throughout history by creating several fictions that are incredibly important to daily life for most of humanity, like, &quot;money&quot;. Profit is just a very easy way to measure created value. One that can be easily taught to the newbies who are pre-conditioned to working within the preferred Foci of the Syndicate.<br /> <br /> But scruples, ethics, morals, etc. are NOT an essential part of the mix to create value and, in fact, can get in the way of doing so, particularly if you want to get things done faster. </div> </div> </div>But the question is not if scruples, ethics, and morals are part of the mix to create value. The question is if they are an important part of the Syndicate. And this is what I meant earlier: when you reduce the organization to a single motivation you are bypassing that entire issue. You are sidelining one of the major places that checks and balances could be and then pointing out that there are no checks and balances.<br /> <br /> Again, no problem if that's they kind of Syndicate you want to portray, but its not the best way to handle the question of if the Syndicate is evil.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, yes, real world business in the sense of capitalism in the sense of competition over limited resources to produce gain ('supply' and 'demand') does inherently have issues in that the bottom will always fall out of it when any participant stops behaving ethically. Starting with the Tragedy of the Commons and moving onwards. To most of the people here it seems to be seen as an inherent bug in the system that they want to wish away. To a lot of very rich people and many economists, it's a design feature, not a flaw. </div> </div> </div>I feel like the qualifier &quot;the bottom will always fall out of it when any participant stops behaving ethically&quot; can be applied to every human system everywhere. Governments, social clubs, courts, sporting events...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T11:48:28-07:00","id":1074255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1074114#post1074114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That doesn't change that how the Syndicate is portrayed completely changes their moral status. So choosing a single negative lens to look at them through isn't as useful as, say, looking at the positive depictions of the Syndicate and seeing how they could be twisted. The latter also avoids the two least interesting options, the squeaky clean Syndicate and the wreched hive of scum and villainy Syndicate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But the question is not if scruples, ethics, and morals are part of the mix to create value. The question is if they are an important part of the Syndicate. And this is what I meant earlier: when you reduce the organization to a single motivation you are bypassing that entire issue. You are sidelining one of the major places that checks and balances could be and then pointing out that there are no checks and balances.<br /> <br /> Again, no problem if that's they kind of Syndicate you want to portray, but its not the best way to handle the question of if the Syndicate is evil.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I feel like the qualifier &quot;the bottom will always fall out of it when any participant stops behaving ethically&quot; can be applied to every human system everywhere. Governments, social clubs, courts, sporting events...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If that's the question then the answer is pretty much an emphatic &quot;No&quot;. That's based on what is actually, physically IN the game materials past and present. With the notable exception being when the Syndicate talks about themselves. Which, in a mortally and ethically compromised organization is worth less than the paper it's written on. So, since the material answers the question shouldn't the problem have been solved by a post answering the first stating that and then we're done? Or were we arguing the point from various points of view? And, if so, doesn't taking extreme positions allow for more full exploration of the topic? At least in the couple of thousands of years we've had rhetoric, it's been held that it does.... <br /> <br /> Someone could just as easily take the &quot;Syndicate promotes the greatest good&quot; position. They will have a ton of material to start with in the Syndicate's material about itself and they will have to start refuting the evidence of the prevalence of bad actors in the group. <br /> <br /> The problem with capitalism as an economic system and the way it develops is that it is more vulnerable to the bottom dropping out when ethics are compromised. There are a number of reasons for this but a simple one that doesn't take a lot of explanation with footnotes is the the fundamental inclusion of competition. Other human systems are not as susceptible to the lack of ethics of individual participants creating a cascade effect.because they are not so fundamentally based on competition. (Like, say, a majority of the forms of government and social organizations which human beings have experimented with, social organizations of all types, etc.) When there is an incentive to exploit when others are not, it usually takes an outside control to create the pressure to disincentivize that. That process doesn't exist internally in capitalism. A beneficent capiialistic system that exists in and of itself with no outside controls would pretty much require a post-scarcity situation. But a capitalistic system and the way in which it fundamentally allocates resources will not result in a post-scarcity situation. (Sorry Syndicate, you lose.... You'll never get where you're going. But the NWO is in the same boat. The hope for humanity lies with the other three....)<br /> <br /> You DO always have to worry about the Tragedy of the Commons unless there is some way to punish those who start taking advantage of the Commons unless the Commons are infinitely exploitable. . <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T07:00:53-07:00","id":1074634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1074255#post1074255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's the question then the answer is pretty much an emphatic &quot;No&quot;. That's based on what is actually, physically IN the game materials past and present. With the notable exception being when the Syndicate talks about themselves. Which, in a mortally and ethically compromised organization is worth less than the paper it's written on. So, since the material answers the question shouldn't the problem have been solved by a post answering the first stating that and then we're done?</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the initial few posts to the question did that just fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1074255#post1074255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or were we arguing the point from various points of view? And, if so, doesn't taking extreme positions allow for more full exploration of the topic? At least in the couple of thousands of years we've had rhetoric, it's been held that it does....</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I thought we were trying to give the OP the most appropriate answer to the given question.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1074255#post1074255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But a capitalistic system and the way in which it fundamentally allocates resources will not result in a post-scarcity situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>They plan to abandon capitalism once they have enough control over humanity to direct human belief so as to make utopian systems acceptable within the bounds of Consensus. Capitalism is the tool they plan to use to take control of humanity. Belief is the tool they plan to use to achieve their actual goals.<br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, what would you propose as an economic system to replace capitalism?<br /> (I'd really like to know as I've toyed with various ideas in my attempts at fiction (emphasis on attempts) but have never arrived at anything without equal or greater potential for problems)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T07:41:23-07:00","id":1074651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1074255#post1074255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that's the question then the answer is pretty much an emphatic &quot;No&quot;. That's based on what is actually, physically IN the game materials past and present. With the notable exception being when the Syndicate talks about themselves. Which, in a mortally and ethically compromised organization is worth less than the paper it's written on. So, since the material answers the question shouldn't the problem have been solved by a post answering the first stating that and then we're done? Or were we arguing the point from various points of view? And, if so, doesn't taking extreme positions allow for more full exploration of the topic? At least in the couple of thousands of years we've had rhetoric, it's been held that it does....<br /> <br /> Someone could just as easily take the &quot;Syndicate promotes the greatest good&quot; position. They will have a ton of material to start with in the Syndicate's material about itself and they will have to start refuting the evidence of the prevalence of bad actors in the group.</div> </div> </div> </div>That kind of rhetoric only works if we are willing to see the positions knocked down. When you set up barriers like discounting what the Syndicate has to say about itself it hamstrings the entire method.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problem with capitalism as an economic system and the way it develops is that it is more vulnerable to the bottom dropping out when ethics are compromised. There are a number of reasons for this but a simple one that doesn't take a lot of explanation with footnotes is the the fundamental inclusion of competition. Other human systems are not as susceptible to the lack of ethics of individual participants creating a cascade effect.because they are not so fundamentally based on competition. (Like, say, a majority of the forms of government and social organizations which human beings have experimented with, social organizations of all types, etc.) When there is an incentive to exploit when others are not, it usually takes an outside control to create the pressure to disincentivize that. That process doesn't exist internally in capitalism. A beneficent capiialistic system that exists in and of itself with no outside controls would pretty much require a post-scarcity situation. But a capitalistic system and the way in which it fundamentally allocates resources will not result in a post-scarcity situation. (Sorry Syndicate, you lose.... You'll never get where you're going. But the NWO is in the same boat. The hope for humanity lies with the other three....) </div> </div> </div>Oh there's competition in every social dynamic. Competition for rank, for status, for influence, etc. Capitalism is open about it, but even the most structured and planned society has people playing politics to get ahead (in whatever form getting ahead takes). So I'd argue it's not that capitalism is more vulnerable to the bottom dropping out, it's that it is more obvious when that happens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You DO always have to worry about the Tragedy of the Commons unless there is some way to punish those who start taking advantage of the Commons unless the Commons are infinitely exploitable. . </div> </div> </div>In counterpoint to the Tragedy of the Commons, though, is the bizarre talent humanity seems to have for making cool stuff out of its own waste. Paper, artificial dyes, raincoats, gasoline, plastics,.. all of these started as ways of reusing our worthless detritus. We really do have an uncanny ability to turn our detritus and our wastelands into the next source of new potential.<br /> <br /> It just lacks a pithy name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T08:19:42-07:00","id":1074663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They plan to abandon capitalism once they have enough control over humanity to direct human belief so as to make utopian systems acceptable within the bounds of Consensus. Capitalism is the tool they plan to use to take control of humanity. Belief is the tool they plan to use to achieve their actual goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I still don't think good and evil are good terms to understand what the Syndicate it's doing, I think that you got yourself into a hole with that one. The idea that Utopy it's so inherently against the Consensus that you should avoid it at all costs, even to the point of disalowing Coincidental efforts in that direction, it's a belief held by the Syndicate, and only them. No one else it's so fanatical with avoiding Paradox. The Conventions didn't avoided Paradox when they were teaching the masses the advantages of gunpowder (while the Guild preffered subtlety). Paradox didn't kill the Craftmasons, it was the Syndicate who acted against them when they started making public their social experiments.<br /> Since belief it's magick, the deeply held anty-utopist belief of the Syndicate acts as an argument against any possibility that they may have to actually reach said utopy. They're called &quot;the guardians of the status quo&quot; for a reason. I would rather put the hopes for Utopy on someone that doesn't wear that moniker with pride.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T08:43:22-07:00","id":1074673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1074663#post1074663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I still don't think good and evil are good terms to understand what the Syndicate it's doing, I think that you got yourself into a hole with that one. The idea that Utopy it's so inherently against the Consensus that you should avoid it at all costs, even to the point of disalowing Coincidental efforts in that direction, it's a belief held by the Syndicate, and only them. No one else it's so fanatical with avoiding Paradox. The Conventions didn't avoided Paradox when they were teaching the masses the advantages of gunpowder (while the Guild preffered subtlety). Paradox didn't kill the Craftmasons, it was the Syndicate who acted against them when they started making public their social experiments.<br /> Since belief it's magick, the deeply held anty-utopist belief of the Syndicate acts as an argument against any possibility that they may have to actually reach said utopy. They're called &quot;the guardians of the status quo&quot; for a reason. I would rather put the hopes for Utopy on someone that doesn't wear that moniker with pride.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said it was a great plan nor a better plan than what the other conventions have. It is simply the plan they are following. Also, they don't think a utopia is impossible. They think it is impossible without first going through certain (possibly unnecessary) steps. It's the limitation of their belief system that they think such a system won't be accepted by consensus right now, but not that it will never be acceptable. They believe they have to do certain specific things before they can make their vision of utopia a part of consensus.<br /> <br /> I personally wouldn't put my hopes for utopia on anything from the current technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-07-2017, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T10:48:14-07:00","id":1074747,"title":"","content":"Yes, well, I think I can get behind that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T11:43:57-07:00","id":1076001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1074651#post1074651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That kind of rhetoric only works if we are willing to see the positions knocked down. When you set up barriers like discounting what the Syndicate has to say about itself it hamstrings the entire method.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh there's competition in every social dynamic. Competition for rank, for status, for influence, etc. Capitalism is open about it, but even the most structured and planned society has people playing politics to get ahead (in whatever form getting ahead takes). So I'd argue it's not that capitalism is more vulnerable to the bottom dropping out, it's that it is more obvious when that happens.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In counterpoint to the Tragedy of the Commons, though, is the bizarre talent humanity seems to have for making cool stuff out of its own waste. Paper, artificial dyes, raincoats, gasoline, plastics,.. all of these started as ways of reusing our worthless detritus. We really do have an uncanny ability to turn our detritus and our wastelands into the next source of new potential.<br /> <br /> It just lacks a pithy name.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are salesmen. Do you believe if you eat at Hardy's you will be fawned on by super-models in bathing suits? That you will be able to drive your Jeep Wrangler to the top of a rock pillar hundreds of feet out from a mesa? That if you wear Axe Body Spray you will be physically attacked by beautiful women? Then why do you believe that the people who invented advertising are telling you the truth about themselves in their internal propaganda? Since the Convention books are written as &quot;fluff&quot; first, you are not getting an evenhanded viewpoint. You are asking us to base the discussion, not just on an unreliable narrator, but a narrator whose job is to lie convincingly.<br /> <br /> So, no, legitimate argumentation would demand that taking their statements for their truth are not good foundations and NOT accepting them, in fact, with rigor doesn't hamstring the argument.<br /> <br /> That's just as much NOT true as it is true, though as products of a culture that exalts competitiveness, we are all too willing to turn a blind eye to the inherent importance of cooperation. In fact, cooperation, overall, is MORE fundamental to a functioning culture or society than competition. And capitalism is probably less open it's internal competitiveness than other institutions that are actually less competitive overall. Unfortunately nothing you are stating actually changes the facts that capitalism as a form of good distribution is much much more prone to things we'd call ethical issues than sharing, barter, redistribution networks, prestige based exchange, etc. Not that those don't have their own issues, but, capitalism has this issue as an inherent bug in it's functionality.<br /> <br /> And the opposite of the Tragedy of the Commons isn't innovating your way out of the mess you've made. That's not what the Tragedy of the Commons is or how it works. The opposite doesn't have a name, you're right, but it would something more like &quot;Communism of Shared Resources&quot; or the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T11:46:16-07:00","id":1076003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1073856#post1073856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fallacy of the Excluded Middle. The options aren't \u201ceither they're overrun by Technophandi or they're shining beacons of hope\u201d. There are options in between those extremes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Touche, but, it is not bad rhetoric to argue from an extreme. In fact, it's good rhetoric to do so. <br /> <br /> Though... probably it would be better if there was someone arguing the other extreme and perhaps some pithy kibitizing from more reasonable middle positions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T11:55:46-07:00","id":1076013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1074634#post1074634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought the initial few posts to the question did that just fine.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well, I thought we were trying to give the OP the most appropriate answer to the given question.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They plan to abandon capitalism once they have enough control over humanity to direct human belief so as to make utopian systems acceptable within the bounds of Consensus. Capitalism is the tool they plan to use to take control of humanity. Belief is the tool they plan to use to achieve their actual goals.<br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, what would you propose as an economic system to replace capitalism?<br /> (I'd really like to know as I've toyed with various ideas in my attempts at fiction (emphasis on attempts) but have never arrived at anything without equal or greater potential for problems)</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the correct answer to the OP is: &quot;Yes they are evil, according to the setting as written currently. Like most evil organizations, they don't see themsleves that way, but, insofar as Mage has an absolute moral compass (e.g. &quot;Nephandi bad&quot;), then overall, despite the inevitable fine-grained exceptions, it's hell evil. The very heart of the worst of evilness there is, since it's so successfully evil. Otherwise, YMMV and it's all up in the air for argument.&quot; <br /> <br /> If you believe their hype, then sure. I bet some of them even believe it. Probably mostly the newbies and some really starry-eyed middle management types with Pangloss issues. On the other hand, we have a continuum from the pre-Order High Guild up through the current Syndicate (in personnel even) that have spend centuries being very successful at accomplishing their goals by pursuing this one thing and steamrolling everything else up into it. Though capitalism has changed in complexity, it hasn't, as a system fundamentally changed in that entire time. In fact, the High Guild = the Syndicate = the development and flourishing of capitalism isn't too far off the mark. So, aside from the propaganda, where does this &quot;new next best thing&quot; fit in. <br /> <br /> You want to see some fun contrasting capitalism and post-capitalism, Eclipse Phase tries to play with those ideas on a large scale (as in &quot;the Solar System&quot; large).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T12:12:21-07:00","id":1076026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1076001#post1076001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are salesmen. Do you believe if you eat at Hardy's you will be fawned on by super-models in bathing suits? That you will be able to drive your Jeep Wrangler to the top of a rock pillar hundreds of feet out from a mesa? That if you wear Axe Body Spray you will be physically attacked by beautiful women? Then why do you believe that the people who invented advertising are telling you the truth about themselves in their internal propaganda? Since the Convention books are written as &quot;fluff&quot; first, you are not getting an evenhanded viewpoint. You are asking us to base the discussion, not just on an unreliable narrator, but a narrator whose job is to lie convincingly.<br /> <br /> So, no, legitimate argumentation would demand that taking their statements for their truth are not good foundations and NOT accepting them, in fact, with rigor doesn't hamstring the argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course it's flawed and you're supposed to take it with a grain of salt. That's a far cry from saying it's &quot;worth less than the paper it's written on.&quot; It may be be sugarcoated but it's also the best view we have into what they think about themselves. The book is supposed to be useful, after all.<br /> <br /> That's the problem with your rhetorical method, not that you are taking the worst case scenario but that you are only allowing for the worst case evidence. <br /> <br /> <br /> As for issues with actual capitalism, I think if we take it much further it would be sidetracking the thread. Suffice to say, I have issues with your depiction and I don't think it encapsulates the way systems and economies can go wrong.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T13:39:13-07:00","id":1076076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1074255#post1074255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. (Sorry Syndicate, you lose.... You'll never get where you're going. But the NWO is in the same boat. The hope for humanity lies with the other three....)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm? How does the hope for humanity lie in the Convention that's centered on the principle of reducing humans to cogs in a machine? Or in the Convention that seeks to deny the soul and promotes the notion that biology is the only thing that matters, that there's no qualitative difference between a man and a dog? Or in the Convention that's the embodiment of colonialism, subjugating and exploiting the Other? If you're going to take worst-case scenarios as the norm, all of the Conventions lose. So do the Traditions, for that matter.<br /> <br /> Also, you claim that the bottom is more likely to fall out of a capitalism-based system than any of the alternatives once ethics are removed, and that the central role of competition is a major reason for this. I respectfully call BS: competition generally acts as a <i>deterrence</i> to corruption in a healthy capitalist economy; and when a capitalist system breaks down it's usually characterized by competition being subverted in some way, be it the emergence of a monopoly or trust or the rise of crony capitalism (i.e., government-supported monopolies).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T14:10:50-07:00","id":1076098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1076013#post1076013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then the correct answer to the OP is: &quot;Yes they are evil, according to the setting as written currently. Like most evil organizations, they don't see themsleves that way, but, insofar as Mage has an absolute moral compass (e.g. &quot;Nephandi bad&quot;), then overall, despite the inevitable fine-grained exceptions, it's hell evil. The very heart of the worst of evilness there is, since it's so successfully evil. Otherwise, YMMV and it's all up in the air for argument.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be using them as a definition for evil rather than defining evil and then showing how they fit into that definition. Evil, as I see it, is defined as profoundly immoral and malevolent. I find them to be immoral but not profoundly so and nowhere near profoundly malevolent. Therefore, not evil. Not very good either, but at least capable of good in some cases. I don't see how &quot;the very heart of the worst of evilness&quot; is there. Are you equating capitalism with evil? That might not be your intended message but that's what most of this sounds like to me. Also, the success of the organization has nothing to do with the organization's being good or evil. What is your measure of evil here? <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1076013#post1076013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you believe their hype, then sure. I bet some of them even believe it. Probably mostly the newbies and some really starry-eyed middle management types with Pangloss issues. On the other hand, we have a continuum from the pre-Order High Guild up through the current Syndicate (in personnel even) that have spend centuries being very successful at accomplishing their goals by pursuing this one thing and steamrolling everything else up into it. Though capitalism has changed in complexity, it hasn't, as a system fundamentally changed in that entire time. In fact, the High Guild = the Syndicate = the development and flourishing of capitalism isn't too far off the mark. So, aside from the propaganda, where does this &quot;new next best thing&quot; fit in.</div> </div> </div> </div>The hype? I've always recognized them as a group that wants to control the world because they think they are best at doing so. They have as much right to control humanity as anyone else... which is not much. Their new next best thing is supposed to come after they can safely control Consensus because they think that even a small amount of paradox in the global economy will screw the world up royally. They have to wait til almost all people are on a cashless system and they can subtly tweak a few numbers here and there to control public opinion regarding what people should spend on (put their faith in). They are centuries away from their goals and feel that hurrying will just screw stuff up. This all still falls squarely in the realm of self interest. What hype? What propaganda?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1076013#post1076013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You want to see some fun contrasting capitalism and post-capitalism, Eclipse Phase tries to play with those ideas on a large scale (as in &quot;the Solar System&quot; large).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've played a game of that and haven't seen how such economies would actually feasibly work without even worse problems than before.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, with regards to your ideas on rhetoric, arguing from an extreme is only really great if you are trying to win a debate rather than trying to seek out actual truth or its closest approximate, which is what I believe we should be doing in a forum such as this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T14:49:14-07:00","id":1076129,"title":"","content":"I'd also point out that manipulating the Consensus is more of an NWO thing than a Syndicate thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T09:20:39-07:00","id":1077018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1076076#post1076076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm? How does the hope for humanity lie in the Convention that's centered on the principle of reducing humans to cogs in a machine? Or in the Convention that seeks to deny the soul and promotes the notion that biology is the only thing that matters, that there's no qualitative difference between a man and a dog? Or in the Convention that's the embodiment of colonialism, subjugating and exploiting the Other? If you're going to take worst-case scenarios as the norm, all of the Conventions lose. So do the Traditions, for that matter.<br /> <br /> Also, you claim that the bottom is more likely to fall out of a capitalism-based system than any of the alternatives once ethics are removed, and that the central role of competition is a major reason for this. I respectfully call BS: competition generally acts as a <i>deterrence</i> to corruption in a healthy capitalist economy; and when a capitalist system breaks down it's usually characterized by competition being subverted in some way, be it the emergence of a monopoly or trust or the rise of crony capitalism (i.e., government-supported monopolies).</div> </div> </div> </div>Because, if you believe the R&amp;D Convetion's hype, they are effectively baseline about human empowerment shading fully into transhumanism. If your stated goal is to &quot;make people better&quot; and, with a lot of hiccups (really nasty and bad hiccups) and handwringing about what better means, you actually have tanglible examples of such, you're doing a better job of making humanity better, unless it's better sheep. The Ascension that is the endless uniformity of a grey mass of undifferentiated identical individuals. <br /> <br /> You are incorrect. REGULATED capitalism can, potentially lead to such things (though, again, since it is inherently competitive, there are going to be issues... vide some societies that AREN'T capitialistic and are also cooperation oriented and you can see the differences). Pure capitalism as such is an inevitable race to the bottom overall. The exceptions will inevitably fail. (Hence, the Tragedy of the Commons... which will always happen, because it only takes ONE dishonest or greedy person without any external control mechanisms in place to throw the system The Virtuous Cycle requires government oversight, cooperation and investment. When any of those falter, it's going to turn into the Vicious Cycle. Even Adam Smith admitted it took God to keep capitalism on course. There is no evidence that, without a strong guiding hand, you ever get capitalism to accomplish anything resembling &quot;public good&quot;. Which is probably (meaning &quot;absolutely certainly&quot;) an initial precondition if the goal is &quot;Mass Ascension.&quot; If your fundamental system mechanics don't actually lead to your stated goal, you're maladaptive at best and, most likely, your stated goals aren't your actual goals, whether that's implicit and there's a lack of awareness or internally explicit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T09:24:13-07:00","id":1077020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1076129#post1076129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also point out that manipulating the Consensus is more of an NWO thing than a Syndicate thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you use this thing called &quot;money&quot; to stay alive, to measure your value in regards to society? Does it measure your ability to affect your environment? Determine how you are treated by society as a whole?<br /> <br /> The Syndicate is so successful at manipulating the Consensus that almost any member of it can't even conceive that there are alternatives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T10:16:26-07:00","id":1077049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1076098#post1076098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You seem to be using them as a definition for evil rather than defining evil and then showing how they fit into that definition. Evil, as I see it, is defined as profoundly immoral and malevolent. I find them to be immoral but not profoundly so and nowhere near profoundly malevolent. Therefore, not evil. Not very good either, but at least capable of good in some cases. I don't see how &quot;the very heart of the worst of evilness&quot; is there. Are you equating capitalism with evil? That might not be your intended message but that's what most of this sounds like to me. Also, the success of the organization has nothing to do with the organization's being good or evil. What is your measure of evil here?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The hype? I've always recognized them as a group that wants to control the world because they think they are best at doing so. They have as much right to control humanity as anyone else... which is not much. Their new next best thing is supposed to come after they can safely control Consensus because they think that even a small amount of paradox in the global economy will screw the world up royally. They have to wait til almost all people are on a cashless system and they can subtly tweak a few numbers here and there to control public opinion regarding what people should spend on (put their faith in). They are centuries away from their goals and feel that hurrying will just screw stuff up. This all still falls squarely in the realm of self interest. What hype? What propaganda?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I've played a game of that and haven't seen how such economies would actually feasibly work without even worse problems than before.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, with regards to your ideas on rhetoric, arguing from an extreme is only really great if you are trying to win a debate rather than trying to seek out actual truth or its closest approximate, which is what I believe we should be doing in a forum such as this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not doing that. Phil Brucato is doing that. He's explicitly doing that. He has the buy in of the other authors of M20 and Onyx Path on that as the most current word on that. He has implicitly rejected the conception of the Syndicate in the Rev Convention Book in both that he really does seem to treat it as pure propaganda and that he has absolutely set out as a &quot;default&quot; setting that the Syndicate is not only &quot;not the good guys&quot; they are the home base for a significant fraction of the worst guys.<br /> <br /> Insofar as Mage has a definition of &quot;evil&quot;, it's explicitly the Nephandi. (Which can lead to a whole host of arguments about a game in which it's stated that &quot;Everything is Relative&quot; then they move on to say &quot;Absolute evil is real and here it is&quot;.) The Nephandi are most successful in the Technocracy as the Technephandi, which, you CAN take or leave, but, unless there's a huge vector change, is going to be an assumption going forward. The dial on how infested with Nephandi the Technocracy is is going to be a Purple Box set up as far as it looks now and &quot;Just as much as any other Faction is not going to be the initial position. And, without reading between the line too much, the Syndicate is the heart and soul of the continuity of that evil influence from the inception of the Order of Reason right up to modern times. (Which makes sense, since, really, they have been fundamentally the same group every way from then until now. The name change is cosmetic when compared to the mix-mastering of OoR Conventions and the massive fundamental underlying ideological shifts that occurred in the Conventions with any apparent continuity). Hells, it seems like they brought it to the table.<br /> <br /> If you were correct about the second, then there would never have been a finanical collapse The Syndicate would never have played chicken with the world economy for fun and profit. There is obviously, at the very least, a difference of ideologies in the Convention currently, with the &quot;Bear&quot; side currently ascendant. If you are correct, there must have been a brutal, ruthless, bloody, mass purge of the others (which is pretty ethically dicey), or all those folks who were 100% behind risking the world economy are still a major component of the Convention, trying to figure out how to bring things back around to their way of thinking.<br /> <br /> Those are the alternatives out there. Considering there have been many, many, many other types of economies out there (to the level that the word &quot;economy&quot; is as meaningless as &quot;religion&quot; as idenitfying a relevant separate concept is in many other cultures), they might work out. They haven't been given the virtue of trying so far on a systemic scale. (Though bits and pieces show through here and there). In fact, some of them are fundamentally just cosmetic sleeves over some very old and very functional systems. Some of which have lasted for so much longer than capitalism as a system that there really isn't even a comparison. Trying to pull oneself out of one's own setting and trying to get a firm grasp on very different ideas from other cultures or periods is not an easy thing to do. It's as difficult to as learning another language to a functional level (and, in fact, can sometimes be very much the same thing.) But &quot;What we've got&quot; isn't even a good measure of &quot;What works well&quot; overall. It's just what we've got. It's our normal. And that very different thing those dude's have is NOT normal. Humans have issues with &quot;not normal&quot; ever equalling &quot;as good&quot; much less &quot;potentially better for certain values of better&quot;.<br /> <br /> And, since you're tossed rhetoric aside, which is one of the better ways we've found to seek out truth (like capitalism is one of the better ways we've found to distribute resources and democracy is one of the better ways we've found to distribute power, not the only ways, but definitely ways that can work and that we are familiar with), what is your proposal for another methodology? Even if all you've done is get more steadfast in your position on the Syndicate, you've had to at least consider there are alternative views and you've had to figure out not just that you don't like them, but now have reasons you can articulate about WHY you don't like them. You might even have broadened your viewpoint of what the Syndicate can be or see that it's a buffet and you can pick what you like for it, either as a whole or for the bits that on stage now.<br /> <br /> Like I've said repeatedly, I am actually using the Syndicate as a major part of my current actual, not theoretical, being played M20 game. And they aren't just this seething shoggoth of pure evil made of thousands of little angry toothy greedy tadpole mages. They just, in fact, became the haven in the storm to the cabal. Of course, they expect some help in return and its going to suck up some of the players into an internal coup within this Amalgam (/family-owned international shipping company). So, are they good guys? Sure. To a point. Are they self-interested and into quid-pro-quo in a ruthless way? Yup. So... I'm not even going to the full-on Technephandi-infested Syndicate norm. At least here (and TBH, not at all in my games. The Union falling on its face is a category of evil all it's own. Just like the Traditions. The Nephandi-infestation dial for my games has typically been &quot;Low&quot; across the board. Independant Nephandi have been the norm when Nephandi do show up. So far, NONE in this chronicle... though they do get talked about.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 04-12-2017, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T10:30:54-07:00","id":1077056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1077018#post1077018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are incorrect. REGULATED capitalism can, potentially lead to such things (though, again, since it is inherently competitive, there are going to be issues... vide some societies that AREN'T capitialistic and are also cooperation oriented and you can see the differences). Pure capitalism as such is an inevitable race to the bottom overall. The exceptions will inevitably fail. (Hence, the Tragedy of the Commons... which will always happen, because it only takes ONE dishonest or greedy person without any external control mechanisms in place to throw the system The Virtuous Cycle requires government oversight, cooperation and investment. When any of those falter, it's going to turn into the Vicious Cycle. Even Adam Smith admitted it took God to keep capitalism on course. There is no evidence that, without a strong guiding hand, you ever get capitalism to accomplish anything resembling &quot;public good&quot;. Which is probably (meaning &quot;absolutely certainly&quot;) an initial precondition if the goal is &quot;Mass Ascension.&quot; If your fundamental system mechanics don't actually lead to your stated goal, you're maladaptive at best and, most likely, your stated goals aren't your actual goals, whether that's implicit and there's a lack of awareness or internally explicit.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'm beginning to get your general arguments with regards to capitalism, I'd still have to argue &quot;not evil&quot;. I see capitalism as a tool, like a knife or a fire... more like a fire. Using unregulated capitalism and then calling it evil is a bit like carelessly lighting fire in your house and then calling it evil when your house burns down.<br /> <br /> I feel I have a clear view of how the Syndicate intends to achieve its goals which involves: First converting money to a state in which the Syndicate does not have to worry too much about physical cash as a variable; Then influencing belief by making predictable, believable increases in profit and savings for those who choose certain things they approve of alongside predictable believable decreases in profit and savings for those who don't; Then as people put more and more &quot;stock&quot; in what the Syndicate desires, focus this belief in a predictable manner to allow for the creation of currently impossible or improbable developments (as opposed to forcing these on a consensus on a regular basis and watching these catch of flop with the occasional massive backlash). These developments would then be what would actually lead to ascension. And this has the pleasant side effect of giving the Syndicate full control of reality.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T11:09:40-07:00","id":1077079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1077049#post1077049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not doing that. Phil Brucato is doing that. He's explicitly doing that. He has the buy in of the other authors of M20 and Onyx Path on that as the most current word on that. He has implicitly rejected the conception of the Syndicate in the Rev Convention Book in both that he really does seem to treat it as pure propaganda and that he has absolutely set out as a &quot;default&quot; setting that the Syndicate is not only &quot;not the good guys&quot; they are the home base for a significant fraction of the worst guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like more info on this if you have it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1077049#post1077049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Insofar as Mage has a definition of &quot;evil&quot;, it's explicitly the Nephandi. (Which can lead to a whole host of arguments about a game in which it's stated that &quot;Everything is Relative&quot; then they move on to say &quot;Absolute evil is real and here it is&quot;.) The Nephandi are most successful in the Technocracy as the Technephandi, which, you CAN take or leave, but, unless there's a huge vector change, is going to be an assumption going forward. The dial on how infested with Nephandi the Technocracy is is going to be a Purple Box set up as far as it looks now and &quot;Just as much as any other Faction is not going to be the initial position. And, without reading between the line too much, the Syndicate is the heart and soul of the continuity of that evil influence from the inception of the Order of Reason right up to modern times. (Which makes sense, since, really, they have been fundamentally the same group every way from then until now. The name change is cosmetic when compared to the mix-mastering of OoR Conventions and the massive fundamental underlying ideological shifts that occurred in the Conventions with any apparent continuity). Hells, it seems like they brought it to the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I gave you the definition of evil I am using and showing you how I fit the ideas into that context. Could you maybe give me a clear definition for your idea of evil? Otherwise, there will be no way to see what exactly falls within your idea of evil or outside of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1077049#post1077049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you were correct about the second, then there would never have been a finanical collapse The Syndicate would never have played chicken with the world economy for fun and profit. There is obviously, at the very least, a difference of ideologies in the Convention currently, with the &quot;Bear&quot; side currently ascendant. If you are correct, there must have been a brutal, ruthless, bloody, mass purge of the others (which is pretty ethically dicey), or all those folks who were 100% behind risking the world economy are still a major component of the Convention, trying to figure out how to bring things back around to their way of thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div>The older book (I only have access to the older syndicate book) seems to suggest there was something of a purge as a whole bunch of the Syndicate members (probably the guys most responsible) went rogue afterwards and were eventually taken care of by Enforcers as the remnants of the Syndicate tried to patch things up again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1077049#post1077049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are the alternatives out there. Considering there have been many, many, many other types of economies out there (to the level that the word &quot;economy&quot; is as meaningless as &quot;religion&quot; as idenitfying a relevant separate concept is in many other cultures), they might work out. They haven't been given the virtue of trying so far on a systemic scale. (Though bits and pieces show through here and there). In fact, some of them are fundamentally just cosmetic sleeves over some very old and very functional systems. Some of which have lasted for so much longer than capitalism as a system that there really isn't even a comparison. Trying to pull oneself out of one's own setting and trying to get a firm grasp on very different ideas from other cultures or periods is not an easy thing to do. It's as difficult to as learning another language to a functional level (and, in fact, can sometimes be very much the same thing.) But &quot;What we've got&quot; isn't even a good measure of &quot;What works well&quot; overall. It's just what we've got. It's our normal. And that very different thing those dude's have is NOT normal. Humans have issues with &quot;not normal&quot; ever equalling &quot;as good&quot; much less &quot;potentially better for certain values of better&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that the whole thing about problems with NOT normal is part of the consensus that needs tweaking.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1077049#post1077049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, since you're tossed rhetoric aside, which is one of the better ways we've found to seek out truth (like capitalism is one of the better ways we've found to distribute resources and democracy is one of the better ways we've found to distribute power, not the only ways, but definitely ways that can work and that we are familiar with), what is your proposal for another methodology? Even if all you've done is get more steadfast in your position on the Syndicate, you've had to at least consider there are alternative views and you've had to figure out not just that you don't like them, but now have reasons you can articulate about WHY you don't like them. You might even have broadened your viewpoint of what the Syndicate can be or see that it's a buffet and you can pick what you like for it, either as a whole or for the bits that on stage now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I rather liked this discussion. I feel the danger of taking an extreme side in terms of seeking the truth in an issue though is the possibility that no one will act as a counterpoint and the result will simply be the extreme idea. I do like the Syndicate mind you but I definitely don't see them as good guys.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1077049#post1077049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I've said repeatedly, I am actually using the Syndicate as a major part of my current actual, not theoretical, being played M20 game. And they aren't just this seething shoggoth of pure evil made of thousands of little angry toothy greedy tadpole mages. They just, in fact, became the haven in the storm to the cabal. Of course, they expect some help in return and its going to suck up some of the players into an internal coup within this Amalgam (/family-owned international shipping company). So, are they good guys? Sure. To a point. Are they self-interested and into quid-pro-quo in a ruthless way? Yup. So... I'm not even going to the full-on Technephandi-infested Syndicate norm. At least here (and TBH, not at all in my games. The Union falling on its face is a category of evil all it's own. Just like the Traditions. The Nephandi-infestation dial for my games has typically been &quot;Low&quot; across the board. Independant Nephandi have been the norm when Nephandi do show up. So far, NONE in this chronicle... though they do get talked about.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Incidentally, this whole discussion has given me an idea for a Syndicate based game.<br /> What was supposed to be a surprise audit of Pentex by the Syndicate Board transformed into a hostile takeover, complete with the eradication of the controlling members of Pentex, much of those below them, and the deaths of a number of Syndicate VPOs. Somehow, against all odds, they've managed to keep the whole affair a secret from the rest of the Technocracy. Absurdly enough, the company is more or less intact and still filled with much of its insanity. The average employee will see this change of leadership as an opportunity for growth. The PCs jobs are to take over the leadership of Pentex and in some cases the identities of some of these former leaders and to &quot;fix&quot; the organization while keeping the whole thing secret from the rest of the known universe. Mainly, I want to see how players with the power to alter reality and the ability to requisition items from the rest of the technocracy so long as they can come up with the proper excuse for its use will try to handle this absurd task.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-12-2017, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T11:42:24-07:00","id":1077100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was supposed to be a surprise audit of Pentex by the Syndicate Board transformed into a hostile takeover, complete with the eradication of the controlling members of Pentex, much of those below them, and the deaths of a number of Syndicate VPOs. Somehow, against all odds, they've managed to keep the whole affair a secret from the rest of the Technocracy. Absurdly enough, the company is more or less intact and still filled with much of its insanity. The average employee will see this change of leadership as an opportunity for growth. The PCs jobs are to take over the leadership of Pentex and in some cases the identities of some of these former leaders and to &quot;fix&quot; the organization while keeping the whole thing secret from the rest of the known universe. Mainly, I want to see how players with the power to alter reality and the ability to requisition items from the rest of the technocracy so long as they can come up with the proper excuse for its use will try to handle this absurd task.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not bad...not going to happen within the metaplot, but metaplot was made so you can break it...I like it.<br /> <br /> However, to truly begin to understand the evilness that it's Pentex, Dimensional Science it's paramount.<br /> <br /> Don't see this as an obstacle, but as a feature. Evil that you can't see can be scary, and while DimSci it's rare outside the VE, it not nonexistant (you could have a few weird agents of the Syndicate with it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T12:37:24-07:00","id":1077135,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that even if no one starts with Dimensional Science, they're going to get it soon enough... or requisition some wonders that might help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-12-2017, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T16:26:39-07:00","id":1078015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1077056#post1077056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I'm beginning to get your general arguments with regards to capitalism, I'd still have to argue &quot;not evil&quot;. I see capitalism as a tool, like a knife or a fire... more like a fire. Using unregulated capitalism and then calling it evil is a bit like carelessly lighting fire in your house and then calling it evil when your house burns down.<br /> <br /> I feel I have a clear view of how the Syndicate intends to achieve its goals which involves: First converting money to a state in which the Syndicate does not have to worry too much about physical cash as a variable; Then influencing belief by making predictable, believable increases in profit and savings for those who choose certain things they approve of alongside predictable believable decreases in profit and savings for those who don't; Then as people put more and more &quot;stock&quot; in what the Syndicate desires, focus this belief in a predictable manner to allow for the creation of currently impossible or improbable developments (as opposed to forcing these on a consensus on a regular basis and watching these catch of flop with the occasional massive backlash). These developments would then be what would actually lead to ascension. And this has the pleasant side effect of giving the Syndicate full control of reality.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, unlike fire, capitalism as tool is built on intent. Which makes it more problematic. <br /> <br /> But that's the point of the Tragedy of the Commons. It doesn't HAVE to happen. But, it's going to happen if there isn't some kind of social, cultural and/or political control that keeps malefactors from acting. Capitalism per se isn't internally regulated. As I've ponted, even Adam Smith assumed a control on this 'perfect system', specifically that it's perfection comes from God himself and that God will make sure the bad guys don't mess up the works. <br /> <br /> If you say that the Syndicate's plan for Ascension is a perfected positive homeostatic feedback loop Virtuous Cycle that rolls up to Mass Ascension.... That sounds fine and dandy. Of course, there are ends and means issues here. This Syndicate is pretty much okay will full on blackness when they think the end is the light. The Road to Hell and all that.... The other thing is exactly what I've been saying, in that, if the Syndicate REALLY wants that, they can't want it all for themselves and fuck the rest of the Conventions. ( &quot;Mass Ascension is OURS!!!!&quot;). That's more like a Syndicate version of a Union Mass Ascension where the NWO does it's part with keeping the appropriate culture in place to keep things from rolling off track, the Progenitors and It-X take care of the endless innovation needed to keep the Cycle going and the VE's take care of the Malthus conundrum(and a few others) by offering continual expansion.<br /> <br /> That's not a bad Technocracy at all. If that's the plan . It if weren't doing such awful things to get there, I might even believe it....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T19:23:47-07:00","id":1078110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1078015#post1078015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Unfortunately, unlike fire, capitalism as tool is built on intent. Which makes it more problematic.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not necessarily more evil in my opinion. Just, more dangerous. I'm guessing maybe you believe in an inherent level of good and evil in all things? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1078015#post1078015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But that's the point of the Tragedy of the Commons. It doesn't HAVE to happen. But, it's going to happen if there isn't some kind of social, cultural and/or political control that keeps malefactors from acting. Capitalism per se isn't internally regulated. As I've ponted, even Adam Smith assumed a control on this 'perfect system', specifically that it's perfection comes from God himself and that God will make sure the bad guys don't mess up the works.</div> </div> </div> </div> To further my analogy. The gas stove in a home could blow it up if misused but I would hardly consider it evil. Even a defective gas stove isn't actually evil. The evil lies elsewhere. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1078015#post1078015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you say that the Syndicate's plan for Ascension is a perfected positive homeostatic feedback loop Virtuous Cycle that rolls up to Mass Ascension.... That sounds fine and dandy. Of course, there are ends and means issues here. This Syndicate is pretty much okay will full on blackness when they think the end is the light. The Road to Hell and all that.... The other thing is exactly what I've been saying, in that, if the Syndicate REALLY wants that, they can't want it all for themselves and fuck the rest of the Conventions. ( &quot;Mass Ascension is OURS!!!!&quot;). That's more like a Syndicate version of a Union Mass Ascension where the NWO does it's part with keeping the appropriate culture in place to keep things from rolling off track, the Progenitors and It-X take care of the endless innovation needed to keep the Cycle going and the VE's take care of the Malthus conundrum(and a few others) by offering continual expansion.</div> </div> </div> </div> I believe that's what their trying to position themselves to do (that Syndicate Version of a Union Mass Ascension) they think it's be a win for everyone on their side but mostly don't like what the NWO seems to have in mind. Humanity gets to end stuff like poverty and all those other hard problems that never seem to go away. The NWO gets a stable world. The progenitors get to improve upon humanity in peace. The other guys get to do their thing. Maybe the Traditions finally get in line. (In theory) <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/33221-is-the-syndicate-evil?p=1078015#post1078015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's not a bad Technocracy at all. If that's the plan . It if weren't doing such awful things to get there, I might even believe it....</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm saying that's the plan. I'm of the opinion that pulling it off is like herding cats. Also, even if they succeed, all the real problems of their setup will pop up later on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}